  beats = {["defias.hideout"]={d={155,92747},b={"Edwin VanCleef"}},["defias.juggernaut"]={d={166},b={"Edwin VanCleef"}},["defias.masons"]={d={135,141,373},b={"Edwin VanCleef"}},["prestor.onyxia"]={},["q1016.2"]={d={1016}},["q1022.6"]={d={1043}},["q1195.3"]={d={1196}},["q120.5"]={d={146}},["q123.3"]={d={147}},["q1274.5"]={d={1249}},["q1480.4"]={d={1482}},["q1483.3"]={d={1094}},["q164.5"]={d={268}},["q165.5"]={d={252}},["q2098.3"]={d={2078}},["q288.4"]={d={290}},["q303.3"]={d={303}},["q358.4"]={d={357}},["q373.5"]={d={393}},["q421.5"]={d={424}},["q437.6"]={d={444}},["q4542.4"]={d={5064}},["q463.2"]={d={463}},["q477.3"]={d={481}},["q4821.5"]={d={5088}},["q488.2"]={d={488}},["q5.2"]={d={5}},["q533.4"]={d={506}},["q533.6"]={d={508}},["q5726.2"]={d={5726}},["q5726.3"]={d={5727}},["q6421.2"]={d={6421}},["q65.7"]={d={166}},["q66.6"]={d={80}},["q66.7"]={d={97}},["q867.3"]={d={875}},["q886.5"]={d={1489}},["q886.6"]={d={1490}},["q94.4"]={d={248}},["q954.5"]={d={957}},["q96392.4"]={d={96391}},["q965.3"]={d={970}},["unsent.lescovar"]={d={434}}},
  recaps = {[219]={k="373",mid={d=350,t="You struck down Edwin VanCleef and found a letter addressed to Baros Alexston in Stormwind. Baros told you of their past in the Stonemasons Guild, where the nobility cheated them and drove VanCleef to rebellion. Seeking answers, you entered the rioting Stockade and executed Bazil Thredd, VanCleef's lieutenant. Warden Thelwater trusted you after this grim act and told you of a mysterious visitor who often met with Thredd. Master Mathias Shaw of SI:7 identified the visitor as Marzon, an assassin serving the corrupt Lord Gregor Lescovar. With VanCleef and Thredd dead, you need undeniable proof of a noble's ties to the Defias Brotherhood. You sought Elling Trias's reluctant aid to unravel the conspiracy. How deep the corruption reaches, and how you can pierce a noble's untouchable standing, remains unknown."},["end"]={d=396,t="You found an unsent letter on Edwin VanCleef that revealed his bitter vendetta against Stormwind's nobility. The trail led from the riotous Stockade to the shadows of Old Town, where you uncovered a conspiracy reaching the city's highest ranks. With covert aid from SI:7 and a daring gnome, you eliminated the corrupt Lord Gregor Lescovar and his assassin in the castle gardens. You silently dismantled the Defias Brotherhood's plot to ruin the kingdom. Though the king was away, Lady Katrana Prestor received your report in Stormwind Keep. Your unspoken justice saved the city from a terrible revenge, while its nobles remained oblivious to how narrowly they had escaped."},before={a=391,t="You found Edwin VanCleef's unsent letter to Baros Alexston, Stormwind's City Architect, on VanCleef's corpse. When you delivered it, Baros recognized the hand of a man consumed by vengeance. He told you how the Stonemasons Guild rebuilt Stormwind after the war, only for the ruling nobles to cheat them of their pay. VanCleef had sparked a riot, then vanished into the wild. To uncover the schemes the mastermind set in motion, Baros sent you to the Stockade to find VanCleef's captive lieutenant, Bazil Thredd. You arrived to find the prison in chaos, its cells open and guards fighting to contain the inmates. Now Warden Thelwater has given you a grim choice: descend into the riot, hunt down the treacherous lieutenant and return with his severed head, or die alongside the other prisoners in the dark."}},[302]={k="65",["end"]={d=166,t="You followed rumors from Lakeshire to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind, seeking the truth behind the thugs driving people from Westfall. The mystery unraveled into a bitter truth: the men terrorizing the countryside were the Stonemasons who rebuilt the capital, pushed to villainy by the kingdom's neglect. You intercepted their dispatches, escorted a terrified traitor through the wilds, and uncovered their hidden stronghold. Deep within, you assassinated their brilliant leader, Edwin VanCleef. Taking his head crippled the ruthless syndicate, and only a glimmer of hope remained that peace might return to the plains."},before={a=166,t="You sought out Wiley the Black in Lakeshire to uncover who led the ruthless gang plaguing Westfall. The indebted rogue surrendered a hurried note detailing a strange alliance with gnolls, kobolds, and goblins. Gryan Stoutmantle caught a whispered mention of the Stonemasons within that missive. Seeking clarity, you ventured to Stormwind to consult Mathias Shaw of SI:7. He revealed that Edwin VanCleef, the talented architect who rebuilt the city after the First War, had turned to crime after a bitter dispute with the King. Stoutmantle demanded proof of this unthinkable betrayal. You intercepted a messenger on the dusty roads near Moonbrook, claiming a letter that confirmed VanCleef’s command. With the mastermind exposed, you escorted a captured traitor through hostile territory, fending off his former comrades until he revealed the gang's secret stronghold. Now, only one grim task remains. Though it is a heavy burden to condemn a man to death, VanCleef must be permanently silenced for the safety of the people, and his head delivered as proof."}},[11]={k="638",mid={d=641,t="You sought Trol'kalar at Vol'jin's demand for the coming war against Zul'Gurub. The legendary sword lay sealed in the tomb of Thoras Trollbane, within Stromgarde's ruins in Arathi Highlands. Three sigils were needed to break the seals, scattered among the city's scavengers and survivors. You took the Sigil of Strom from the Syndicate, then hunted the Stromgarde militia and gathered eleven shattered fragments of the Sigil of Thoradin from their defenders. The shaman Tor'gan forged those pieces into a whole. Two keys were now yours, but the final sigil remained hidden in unknown hands somewhere across the highlands. Until you found it, the tomb stayed sealed."},["end"]={d=646,t="You scoured Stromgarde's crumbling ruins and took ancient sigils from thieves, cavalrymen, and a desperate human prince. With the shattered wards restored, you broke the seal on Thoras Trollbane's tomb and claimed the legendary blade Trol'kalar from the stone hands. You delivered humanity's most feared weapon to Zengu, shifting the balance of power forever. Strom's once mighty bloodline is broken, and the Darkspear hold the key to conquering Zul'Gurub's steamy jungles."}},[19]={k="991",["end"]={d=1046,t="You found Teronis's corpse among the murlocs and took up his unfinished work. From corrupted treants and slaughtered druids, you gathered the scattered pieces of Dartol's rod. You reforged the artifact and awakened its magic at a hidden shrine, then used its power to walk among the furbolgs in disguise. You gained the trust of Krolg, an uncorrupted outcast, and struck down the vicious chieftain Ran Bloodtooth. When you returned Ran Bloodtooth's severed skull to Raene Wolfrunner, you ensured Teronis did not die in vain and brought the Sentinels a hard-won victory."},mid={d=1027,t="You answered Raene Wolfrunner's plea to find her missing friend Teronis. At Lake Falathim's shrine, you found his broken body, slain by the murlocs that claim the waters, and took up his cause. You recovered his journal and the gem he sought, then followed his notes to Shael'dryn, the dryad at her moonwell. She guided you through Ashenvale to reforge Dartol's Rod, an evil wizard's creation Teronis believed could slow the furbolg attacks. Near Felwood, you battled twisted treants for a hidden chest. In Dor'Danil's ruins, you searched for the final fragment once guarded by murdered druids. Now the shattered rod's pieces lie before Shael'dryn. Whether she can mend such dark magic remains unknown."}},[21]={k="1010",["end"]={d=1035,t="You crossed Ashenvale to save a stricken child, bringing Orendil Broadleaf every remedy he could devise. You gathered herbs among the Forsaken-infested ruins of Bathran's Haunt and sought Elune's Tear in the waters of Iris Lake, but these only slowed her sickness. You then took frosted dust from the Ruins of Stardust to break her fever. At Fallen Sky Lake, you slew the Shadethicket Oracle and pried a powerful moonstone from its grasp. When you delivered it to Pelturas Whitemoon in Astranaar, young Relara regained her strength, and her father's hope was restored."}},[22]={k="6382",["end"]={d=247,t="You traveled from the Barrens to test your strength in Ashenvale's wilderness. At Splintertree Post, Senani Thunderheart challenged you to hunt three legendary creatures. You tracked and defeated the great bear Ursangous and the nightsaber Shadumbra in the dense forest. Then you hunted Sharptalon, a fierce hippogryph that often attacked the local peons. You struck down all three powerful animals and claimed their trophies, proving yourself a true hunter. With your strength shown, the frontier was safer for the Horde, and your bravery was bound for the campfire songs."}},[23]={k="6564",["end"]={d=6565,t="You found a damp, crumpled note that exposed the Twilight's Hammer plot to gather crystals radiating with water magic. They meant to empower their aquamancers and placate Aku'Mai, hoping to restore the Old Gods' chaotic reign. When you brought the note to Je'neu Sancrea, you learned Lorgus Jett had orchestrated the plot. You hunted him through the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps and slew him. Back in Zoram'gar, you delivered the news. The Twilight's Hammer ambition was broken, and the Old Gods' destructive forces remained contained for now."},before={a=6565,t="You found a damp, crumpled note whose poor handwriting revealed a sinister plot. Priestesses gathered crystals filled with water elementals' spirits to empower aquamancers in their dark summonings. They meant to appease Aku'Mai and bring about an age ruled by the ancient, chaotic Old Gods. You took the note to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar, giving a name to the unseen enemy. He identified Lorgus Jett, a follower of the Twilight's Hammer, as the architect of the trouble. The cult served long-defeated creatures of chaos and destruction, with no understanding of nature's spirits. Knowing the danger and his own weakness, Je'neu Sancrea charged you with stopping the cultist. You must now venture into Blackfathom Deeps, find Lorgus Jett, and end his life. Only when the deed is done can you return to Zoram'gar."}},[24]={k="1016",["end"]={d=1017,t="You focused a divining scroll with bracers gathered from corrupted water elementals. It revealed Sarilus Foulborne, an undead mage conjuring filth from Dreadmist Peak in the Barrens. Sentinel Velene Starstrike sent you into enemy territory to stop his deliberate destruction of the forest. You climbed the peak and killed him, then returned with his severed head. His arrogant laughter was silenced, and the sacred pools were spared further rot. The Horde had seen what awaited those who earned the Sentinels' wrath."}},[25]={k="25",["end"]={d=824,t="You cleared the Talondeep Path, ending the elemental blockade at Mystral Lake. The frenzied water elementals had brought travel to a standstill. While scouting the gazebo overlooking the nearby Alliance outpost, you found a glowing, tainted globe among the elemental remains. You brought the foul artifact to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, knowing it held the key to the lake's madness. He sent you to Zoram'gar Outpost, where Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring recognized the defiled source of elemental power. He took the relic into his order's care, offering hope that the creeping corruption might finally be stopped."},before={a=824,t="You reached Mystral Lake to reopen the paths between Ashenvale and Stonetalon. After you cut down the raging water elementals, the transport routes were clear, and you scouted a gazebo to spy on nearby Alliance forces. In the bloody aftermath, you found something more troubling than an elemental uprising. From a fallen creature's shattered remains, you recovered a brightly glowing, corrupted globe of water. You took the foul object to Splintertree Post, but Mastok Wrilehiss knew little about such afflictions. He sent you onward, trusting the Earthen Ring's knowledge of the elements and ancient legends. Now you are bound for the coast of the Zoram Strand and Zoram'gar Outpost. There, you hope to find Je'neu Sancrea and bring him the befouled globe, so he can uncover what it means."}},[28]={k="1022",["end"]={d=1044,t="You traced Ashenvale's howling wolf-men to Velinde Starsong, a priestess who had vanished with a mysterious tome. Her trail led you across the ocean, from Ratchet to the southern jungle, then to Duskwood's perpetual gloom. There, you fought beside the Carevin family against the fierce beasts Velinde had unwittingly unleashed. Deep in an overrun mine, you uncovered her grim end. When you returned to the Sentinels, you carried the truth: Velinde had perished, and the powerful Scythe of Elune was lost to her people."},mid={d=1039,t="You found the Tome of Mel'Thandris in a ruined shrine, where savage wolf-men called through the gloom. Its pages showed Priestess Velinde Starsong receiving the Scythe of Elune, a strange artifact. Seeking answers, you learned she had vanished while fighting the demonic presence in the northern forests. With a key, you opened a heavy chest in the Sentinels' bunkhouse and read her old journals. They told of her sudden departure, so you followed her trail across the hostile, sun-baked Barrens to Ratchet, a goblin port. Now you stand before the dockmaster and his dusty ledgers. Did Velinde sail for Blackwater Cove, and what became of her?"}},[38]={k="861",["end"]={d=873,t="You left Mulgore and tested your worth across the Barrens. From the Crossroads to Camp Taurajo, you sharpened your cunning against the dry plains' beasts. You bested the elusive Echeyakee and the relentless Ishamuhale, learning the wild's honor. You survived thunder lizards' crushing footfalls and the fury of thunderhawks before reaching the human-held coast. There, you plunged into the waters and struck down Isha Awak, the Deep Doom. Claiming its heart, you absorbed the mighty terror's solemn pride. You had arrived as eager prey and become an apex predator."},mid={d=881,t="Your path as a hunter began in Mulgore, where Skorn Whitecloud saw your wanderlust. You proved your resolve against the flatland prowlers, then Melor Stonehoof sent you to the Barrens to harden your spirit. At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn put your mettle to the test. You culled nuisance plainstriders, gathered sturdy zhevra hooves, and tracked deadly savannah prowlers through tall grasses. As your strength grew, you earned the right to challenge Echeyakee, the fiercest of the savannah cats. Among ancient kodo bones, you sounded a horn and summoned Whitemist. You claimed victory and carried his merciful spirit with you. The great white beast has fallen, but your path continues. What prey waits in the dry plains, and what trials will Sergra demand of you next?"}},[39]={k="886",["end"]={d=914,t="You journeyed to the Barrens to trace a strange power rising from the earth. Beneath the oases, you found fissures that breathed unnatural life into the wastes and twisted the beasts that drank there. Your trail led to Thunder Bluff, where you learned the Druids of the Fang were the power's source. They had once sought to heal the land, but lost their way in a dark slumber and tried to reshape the world into a nightmare. In the Wailing Caverns, you defeated their four leaders and claimed their dream gems. The terrible visions shattered, and you saved the land from a cursed future."},before={a=1489,t="You met Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads, sent by the druids of Thunder Bluff to investigate a strange power in the Barrens. At the Forgotten Pools, you found a bubbling fissure beneath the water. You then cast dead seeds into another fissure at the Stagnant Oasis, hoping to understand the phenomenon, and watched impossible life spring from nothing. The growth was miraculous, but unnatural. You hunted the snapjaws gathering at the oases and brought back their shells. They revealed a terrible taint that confused the land, leaving the soil caught in a waking dream. Now you know the Wailing Caverns are the source of the corruption. Before you can enter that dangerous place, you must return to the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Hamuul Runetotem, the elder druid, awaits you there and is ready to offer his wise counsel."}},[43]={k="887",["end"]={d=888,t="You fought the Southsea Freebooters who plagued the waters south of Ratchet, thinning their ranks of brigands and cannoneers. When Gazlowe suspected them of intercepting his trade fleet cargo, you took his ledger to Wharfmaster Dizzywig, who confirmed the loss. You returned to the pirates' camp and fought through them to reclaim what they had stolen. There, you recovered the delicate telescopic lens Gazlowe needed to complete his observatory and his missing shipment of boots. Returning the goods struck a blow against the pirates' raiding operation and proved your worth to Ratchet's goblins."}},[44]={k="894A",["end"]={d=902,t="You reached the Venture Company research facility near the Sludge Fen and found a control console alive with erratic lights. After shutting off its valves and silencing the machinery, you pried the needed key from Tinkerer Sniggles. You unlocked the console, worked through its tangle of wires, and pulled the samophlange from its housing. Then you carried the mysterious device back to Sputtervalve in Ratchet. Its true function still eludes you, and the Tinkers' Union in Undermine is set to dissect it and uncover what the Venture Company sought to hide."}},[45]={k="894H",["end"]={d=3924,t="You pried the samophlange from its console at a Venture Company research site after shutting down the valves and taking a key from Tinkerer Sniggles. You brought it to Sputtervalve, who broke it, then carried it to Wenikee Boltbucket for repairs and scavenged nugget slugs to help her. When her work failed, you took the scrap to Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar. You hunted down Boss Copperplug and gathered his scattered manual pages, giving Rilli the knowledge to mend the machine. Now the device rests in capable hands, though its true nature remains unknown."},mid={d=902,t="You traveled far north, southwest of the Sludge Fen, at Sputtervalve's direction and found a Venture Company research facility. There, you hunted a strange device called a samophlange. With an operating manual, you breached the chaotic control console and shut off the fuel, regulator, and main control valves. The mechanism remained locked. You took the console key from Tinkerer Sniggles, drained the terminal's power, and reached into a nest of tangled wire to pull the samophlange from its housing. You carried it back to Ratchet and gave it to Sputtervalve for study before its journey to the Tinkers' Union in Undermine. As Sputtervalve examined the scavenged machinery, the samophlange's true purpose remained unknown."}},[48]={k="867",["end"]={d=1060,t="You answered Darsok Swiftdagger's call at the Crossroads and set out to bleed the harpy threat dry. You culled the Witchwing flock in the northwest, then entered the Dry Hills to dismantle their command. Darsok revealed that Serena Bloodfeather had driven the attacks to avenge her fallen sister. You severed the matriarch's head and ended her vendetta. Your violent work echoed beyond the Barrens. You carried the news to Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in the caves of Malaka'Jin, ending a bitter feud that began with Rexxar long ago. With the Bloodfeather lineage extinguished, Horde caravans could travel safely once more."}},[49]={k="850",["end"]={d=4021,t="You hunted the Kolkar centaurs across the Barrens' dry plains and cut down their rising chieftains. You claimed the heads of Barak Kodobane, Verog the Dervish, and Hezrul Bloodmark, fracturing their leadership. Your victories drove a desperate retaliation: a vengeful host marched from Desolace to assault the Horde bunkers. You met the invaders head-on, shattered their ranks, and felled Warlord Krom'zar. When you tore a scrap from his fallen banner, the centaur invasion ended. You secured the land, and tales of your fierce defense would reach Thrall himself."}},[51]={k="865",["end"]={d=1491,t="You gathered horns from sunscale scytheclaws across the Barrens for Mebok Mizzyrix. He hoped they would help him brew a concoction of pure intellect, but his first experiment failed. He then sent you into the depths of the Wailing Caverns to take Wailing Essence from ectoplasmic creatures. Mebok believed the strange substance caused the unnatural growth spreading through the land. You placed the volatile essence in his eager hands, so he could craft his new drink. Your part in his reckless scheme was done, and Mebok was left to chase his fortune."},before={a=1491,t="You hunted sunscale scytheclaws across the sun-baked Barrens and gathered their horns for Mebok Mizzyrix, an ambitious goblin in Ratchet. He believed the beasts had a unique cunning and planned to crush their crowns into beverages that would elevate the mind. He hoped to grow vastly wealthy from the elixir, but it failed to bring any new brilliance. Seeking a stronger ingredient, Mebok turned to the unusual plants and animals spreading across the land. He now suspects Wailing Essence causes these unnatural changes. His first attempt failed, yet he sent you on a darker path to save his enterprise. You traveled west, leaving open skies for the suffocating gloom of the Wailing Caverns. There, formless, ectoplasmic creatures gather in echoing tunnels. You must hunt them and harvest the shimmering essence they harbor."}},[57]={k="6562",["end"]={d=6563,t="You carried Tsunaman's warning across the land to Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale, where Je'neu Sancrea sent you into Blackfathom Deeps. You pried glowing sapphires from the cavern walls and fought the naga who sought to hoard them. Then you delivered the stones safely to Je'neu, keeping their potent water magic from enemy hands. Whatever dark arcane rituals the naga meant to fuel with that raw elemental power, their schemes were shattered upon the shore."},before={a=6562,t="Tsunaman gave you an urgent call about a distant ally in desperate need of your aid. He sent you to Je'neu Sancrea, who awaited assistance far away at the Zoram'gar Outpost. You left familiar lands behind for Ashenvale, the ancient, shadowed woods of a vast night elf forest sprawling north of the rugged Stonetalon mountains. Reaching the western shores of the Zoram Strand meant a demanding journey through the treacherous passes of Windshear Crag or across the sun-scorched Barrens. Either path led deep into hostile, heavily contested territory, where danger lurked at every turn. Now you prepared to cross the untamed wilderness to the remote coastal outpost. The road was long and arduous, and a grave warning stayed with you: be careful upon the strand, where forces would not take kindly to your presence."}},[58]={k="1198",["end"]={d=1200,t="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass sent you after the missing scout, Argent Guard Thaelrid. You tracked him into the corrupted depths of Blackfathom Deeps, along the coasts of Ashenvale, and found him weakened. There, you uncovered the truth behind the naga and the Twilight's Hammer: Aku'Mai, a servant of an Old God, had claimed a tainted Moon Well in Elune's ancient temple. You struck down Twilight Lord Kelris, the cult's ruthless leader, ending his horrific sacrifices. Then you carried his severed head to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus. The Argent Dawn had won a quiet victory against the terrible evil."},before={a=1198,t="You met Dawnwatcher Shaedlass, an agent of the Argent Dawn, to hear the dark rumors from Ashenvale's coasts. The order watched the unholy union of the Twilight's Hammer and the sinister naga within Blackfathom Deeps. Shaedlass had sent a scout into those caverns to learn more of the spreading shadow, but weeks passed and Argent Guard Thaelrid never returned with his report. With her other forces scattered across the fractured land to face pressing matters, the search fell to you. You listened as the weary Dawnwatcher recounted the long silence from her missing operative. Now you stood at the edge of Blackfathom Deeps, staring into its damp, echoing halls. You had to venture inside, find Argent Guard Thaelrid, and give him whatever aid he might need against the darkness gathered there."}},[59]={k="6344",["end"]={d=6343,t="You answered a call in Darnassus, then sought out Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village. She tasked you as her courier, carrying a peculiar collection of oversized fish bones across the sea to Laird in Auberdine. Laird was shocked by their massive scale, confirming that sea life clinging to Teldrassil was growing far larger than anything along the mainland coast. You returned to Nessa with Laird's suspicion that the great tree might be warping nearby wildlife. The true cause remained hidden, while villagers were content to harvest the uncanny riches the waters provided."}},[60]={k="983",["end"]={d=1003,t="You gathered beast parts across the wilds to help Wizbang Cranktoggle maintain his Buzzboxes around Auberdine. With each repair, the voice crackling over the transmission grew thicker and more slurred. In the end, you learned the truth: you had never been tending communication relays. Your work supplied an illicit brewing operation hidden beneath the noses of the nightelves, distilling the liquor that fueled Wizbang Cranktoggle's drunken revelry."}},[61]={k="954",["end"]={d=957,t="Sent by Thundris Windweaver to Bashal'Aran, you sought the blue aura demons avoided. In the ruins, you found Asterion, a spectral being trapped in eternal torment. You hunted grells and their satyr masters, then claimed the ancient seal that bound him. When you plunged it into Ameth'Aran's blue flames, his chains shattered. Asterion walked the forests freely for the first time since Queen Azshara's reign. His release brought a chilling realization: he sensed that his ancient jailor, Athrikus, still lived. Asterion's long despair had kindled into a burning desire for vengeance."}},[64]={k="4811",["end"]={d=4813,t="You sought a strange red crystal east of Auberdine, where hostile moonkin gathered in the mountains. At Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea's behest, you washed the anomaly in pure moonwell water. Its potent magic cleared the opaque surface, revealing shattered bones and a humanoid jaw trapped within the impenetrable lattice. You brought the grim revelation back to Auberdine for the council's judgment. Whatever foul influence crept down from Felwood to twist the moonkin, its source remained locked within the crimson stone, a silent threat over the distant eastern ridge."}},[65]={k="730",["end"]={d=943,t="You sought Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker's crew in Darkshore and found Archaeologist Hollee terrified for Prospector Remtravel. You ventured south, guarding the oblivious prospector from horrible golems until he unearthed a mysterious fossil. You returned it to Darnassus and learned of a matching discovery across the sea. In Menethil Harbor, you found Archaeologist Flagongut, then hunted through the Wetlands. You recovered his swallowed relic from savage raptors and retrieved the original fossil from Prospector Whelgar. With the Stone of Relu and both fossils together, the eager scholar began deciphering the forgotten powers locked within the ancient rock."}},[66]={k="984",["end"]={d=990,t="You uncovered the Blackwood furbolgs' madness as taint spread through Darkshore. To safeguard Auberdine, you thinned their ranks, then gathered moonstalker pelts for Terenthis to craft a magical cloak. Its illusion hid you as you followed Grimclaw past the corrupted beasts and found Volcor wounded in a cave. You fought beside him through the beasts and back to the road. Your victories gave Auberdine hope and proved your strength. Sentinel Selarin then sent you south to Astranaar to bring much-needed aid to Raene Wolfrunner against the corruption gripping Ashenvale."}},[67]={k="947",["end"]={d=951,t="You gathered fungi for Barithras Moonshade behind Cliffspring Falls, where a sinister presence emerged. The Ancient Onu guided you to the Master's Glaive, and there you found the Twilight's Hammer cult seeking the residual power of a fallen lord. You searched their camp and barely escaped the maddening grip of a twisted tome, tearing away one cursed page. In its chaotic scrawls, Onu saw the cult's true design: to use elven magic to revive their ancient masters. You unearthed faded relics from the ruins of Mathystra, securing the key to understanding how they planned to exploit this power."}},[68]={k="965",mid={d=970,t="You searched for a missing scout after leaving Auberdine. Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze feared the worst. Near the Tower of Althalaxx, you found Balthule Shadowstrike watching warlocks gather outside its walls. Soiled parchments taken from their bodies named the Cult of the Dark Strand. You carried Balthule's hurried warning south to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale Forest, where you found Delgren the Purifier, a paladin. Seeing the threat, he sent you to strike the cultists at Ordil'Aran and seize a corrupted relic. You returned with a glowing soul gem pulsing with dark magic. Delgren is studying its enchantments, but the secret of the cult's power and whatever evil lies trapped inside the gem remain unknown."},["end"]={d=981,t="You found warlocks gathering at the Tower of Althalaxx while seeking Balthule Shadowstrike in Darkshore. You carried their foul parchments south into Ashenvale and joined Delgren the Purifier against the Cult of the Dark Strand. You shattered the captured soul gems, executed the orc warlock Ilkrud Magthrull, and purged the satyr-held camps. Then you climbed the lightning-struck tower and killed the cult's leader, Athrikus Narassin. His death scattered the cult and broke its demonic grip. The forests were safe again, and the paladin offered his blessing for your deeds."}},[70]={k="2098",["end"]={d=2078,t="Threshadons sank Gelkak Gyromast's ship off Darkshore, costing the pirate his vessel and first mate. The key to reactivate his mechanical crewman shattered on the rocks, and raging crawlers, ferocious foreststriders, and murlocs swallowed its fragments. You hunted the beasts and reclaimed the pieces, then restored the tool and found the stranded companion. After powering him up, you brought him back to take revenge on the local murloc chief. You reunited a captain with his metal friend and earned Gelkak Gyromast's salty respect."}},[77]={k="1437",["end"]={d=1440,t="You found an unsent letter and brought it to Baros Alexston, exposing a hidden threat. He sent you to Mathias Shaw, who revealed that a captive named Bazil Thredd was commanding the prison riots. After speaking with Warden Thelwater, you entered the violent cellblocks. You fought through the raging inmates, tracked down Thredd, and killed him. With his defeat, the rebellion was shattered, and the dangerous plot festering in the heart of the city was brought to an end."}},[78]={k="1453",["end"]={d=1467,t="You left the Stonetalon Mountains and crossed the bleak wastes of Desolace in search of work. By Roetten Stonehammer's advice, you followed the northern peaks to Nijel's Point, a secluded refuge. There you met Kreldig Ungor and offered your services to the Reclaimers. The journey earned you a place among them. In this troubled land, people lose cherished relics and even their kin, and you joined a band willing to recover anything for the right coin."}},[84]={k="182",["end"]={d=420,t="You answered Grelin Whitebeard's call to drive trolls from a cave in Coldridge Valley. When a brute stole his journal, you braved the frost to reclaim it. The immediate threat was handled, and Grelin finished his report. He trusted you to carry his findings to his brother, so you crossed a tunnel swarming with savage troggs and reached Kharanos with the missive. Senir Whitebeard now has the document in hand. Grelin's lack of tact might offend the Senate, but the truth of the dangers lurking in the snow is finally bound for Ironforge."}},[92]={k="96392",["end"]={d=96393,t="You met Earthseer Farsen in Dun Morogh, and he showed you a grim vision of Dark Iron dwarves gathering. Near Ironband's Compound, you struck at their spies and found a map among their belongings. It marked hidden tunnels converging beneath Ironforge itself. You pressed into the cavernous depths of Old Ironforge, fought through the Hall of Thanes, and slew their commander, Durgen Dirgehammer. You brought his head to King Magni Bronzebeard, exposing the subterranean invasion. With the dwarven capital spared, the king's guards moved to seal the breaches and secure the lower vaults."}},[93]={k="96408",["end"]={d=96393,t="You met Earthseer Farsen at a lonely campfire above Gol'Bolar Quarry, where he showed you Dark Iron spies infesting Dun Morogh. You slaughtered scouts at Ironband's Compound and found a map revealing a more sinister plot. Its jagged runes showed hidden tunnels converging directly beneath Ironforge. You descended into the Hall of Thanes beneath the ancient city and struck down the invasion's commander, Durgen Dirgehammer. When you delivered his severed head to King Magni Bronzebeard, you exposed the unseen enemy. Now royal guards will seal the cavernous breaches and secure the dwarven capital against the darkness below."}},[94]={k="637",["end"]={d=700,t="You brought a waterlogged envelope from the icy depths to Sara Balloo, then carried her plea to Ironforge. King Magni Bronzebeard could not return her husband from the Twisting Nether, and the sacrifices of his people weighed heavily on him. He chose to honor Sully Balloo in stone. You hauled fine Alterac Granite from the ruins of Lordaeron to Darrow Hill in Hillsbrad, where Grand Mason Marblesten carved the tribute. No monument could restore a lost life, but Sully Balloo's stone memorial now honors the brave soldier who gave everything for the Alliance."}},[95]={k="792",["end"]={d=924,t="You uncovered a dark taint in the Valley of Trials, striking down familiars and taking a medallion from the Burning Blade. Across Durotar, you hunted the cult's agents, slew the warlock Fizzle Darkstorm, and gathered searing collars from cultists inside Skull Rock. The trail led through Orgrimmar to the Barrens, where you carried a volatile power stone high atop Dreadmist Peak. At a fiery altar, you shattered the Demon Seed and severed the cult's connection to the Burning Legion. Its destruction sent a shockwave through the unseen world. Durotar is safe for now, but hidden forces surely know you broke their prize."},mid={d=806,t="You began in the Valley of Trials under Zureetha Fargaze's guidance, as she sensed a dark taint. In a nearby cave, you faced a coven of the Burning Blade, slew their Vile Familiars, and took the Burning Blade Medallion, alive with black magic. Fearing the cult might be only a herald, you carried word of it to Sen'jin Village. Master Gadrin said his home was safe, but the cult's dark influence had already taken root across the waters on the Echo Isles. At Razor Hill, you warned Orgnil Soulscar of the rising threat. His inquiries led you to Thunder Ridge, where you tracked down and slew the goblin warlock Fizzle Darkstorm, then returned with his severed claw. You struck a heavy blow, but how far the cult's reach extends remains unknown."}},[97]={k="5",["end"]={d=240,t="You found Jitters hiding in a ghost town, hungry after weeks of eating weeds. You knew he craved Dusky Crab Cakes from the Scarlet Raven Tavern, so you went to Darkshire to see Chef Grual. The cook told you the famous cakes were made from Venom Web Spiders. You hunted the creatures in the northern foothills and gathered their gooey legs. Grual fried the strange meat with his hidden spices, and you carried the dish back to the ruined town. You gave it to Jitters, and the disguised meal finally eased his hunger and brought the terrified man a little comfort in the darkness."}},[98]={k="164",["end"]={d=55,t="You followed a shadowy witness across Duskwood and uncovered a tragic tale of murder by the Dark Riders. The trail led to Jitters, a terrified man, and a journal that exposed the necromancer Morbent Fel. To break the wizard's protective magic, you recovered Lightforge Iron from a sunken ship in the Wetlands and had it forged into a blessed weapon in Stormwind. With that holy steel, you stormed Morbent Fel's lair above the Raven Hill cemetery and struck him down. The Dark Riders remained at large, but you delivered vengeance for Sven Yorgen and dealt a mighty blow against the evils plaguing the land."},mid={d=268,t="You brought supplies to Sven Yorgen's camp in Duskwood and learned that Dark Riders from Deadwind Pass had slaughtered his family. At his abandoned farm, you found a dirt-stained journal buried by a shadowy witness to the massacre. In Darkshire, you traced the book's origins by questioning Madame Eva, Clerk Daltry, and Tavernkeep Smitts. They remembered a terrified stranger fleeing west toward Raven Hill. You tracked him down and found Jitters, the journal's nervous author. Afraid of Sven's wrath, Jitters gave you his completed journal rather than face him. Its pages revealed a vital lead: the murderous Dark Riders had spoken with the wizard Morbent Fel at the Forlorn Rowe. What the phantom riders wanted, and what role the dark wizard played in their schemes, remained unknown."}},[99]={k="165",mid={d=156,t="You found Abercrombie alone in his shack near the Raven Hill cemetery, unable to travel the dangerous roads. Elaine Carevin had sent you to check on him, and you took up the frail hermit's errands in Darkshire. Madame Eva sent you to Blind Mary, a tragic spirit, for Ghost Hair Thread. With a spectral comb, you gathered her hair despite the weeping ghost's horror at her monstrous state. Abercrombie welcomed the strange thread, then asked for Zombie Juice to warm his blood. Tavernkeep Smitts needed rot blossoms to brew the strong liquor, so you gathered them from the skulls of roaming skeletons. You now had the macabre ingredients, but what Abercrombie meant to do with these sinister supplies remained unknown."},["end"]={d=253,t="You helped Abercrombie, an old hermit, gather thread spun from ghost hair, strong liquor brewed from rot blossoms, and the ribs of fallen ghouls. Though he called them simple favors, your kindness aided a madman. Sirra Von'Indi translated his ancient letter for the mayor, revealing Abercrombie as the legendary Embalmer, who plotted doom for Darkshire. To undo your mistake, you sought his wife Eliza's grave. You tore the Embalmer's beating heart from her cursed chest, broke his dark magic, and secured a powerful defense for the town."}},[101]={k="174",["end"]={d=181,t="You brought Viktori Prism'Antras in Darkshire a simple bronze tube for his strange device, built to pierce the heavens. To give it a polished surface that could catch the light, you sought Blind Mary and wrested her abandoned looking glass from a roaming Insane Ghoul in the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery. Then you descended into the ogre mound in southern Duskwood and struck down Zzarc'Vul for his monocle, the massive lens the device needed. The contraption now stands complete. Viktori searches the distant stars for truths beyond magic that might explain the creeping blight upon the forest."}},[102]={k="173",["end"]={d=223,t="You entered the woods to prove yourself worthy of Master Carevin's cause in Darkshire. In Brightwood Grove, you struck down the Nightbane Shadow Weavers, then faced the Dark Runners overrunning the Rotting Orchard. The worgen kept coming, driven by an unknown dark power. Near their bonfires and caves, you fought the deadly Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones. Your efforts earned Calor's respect and his official recommendation. When you presented it to Master Carevin, he welcomed you into his crusade. Those harrowing trials forged you into a trusted weapon against the demons and undead threatening the realm."}},[103]={k="66",["end"]={d=98,t="You followed a chilling vision to a phantom, searching Darkshire's registries, Moonbrook's abandoned schoolhouse and a Goldshire inn. At a butchered family's estate, you pieced together shredded journal pages and matched the handwriting to the killer. Stalvan Mistmantle was the monster behind the gruesome slaughter. You faced the lunatic at his cottage in the woods and ended his depraved life. When you returned his family ring to Madame Eva, hope came to Duskwood, and his bloodthirst was finally ended."},mid={d=72,t="A dark omen began your search for Stalvan. Madame Eva, the mystic, felt an unnatural chill in her veins and saw death waiting for her granddaughter, Alyssa. She gave you only a name. You went to Clerk Daltry and the town records, which pointed you to an abandoned schoolhouse in Moonbrook. There, an unsent letter lay in an old footlocker. Your trail led to Innkeeper Farley in Goldshire, where you learned of a terrified messenger who fled into a storm, leaving behind correspondence bound for the Canal District in Stormwind. You followed that lead to Caretaker Folsom, haunted by the memory of a gruesome massacre. You opened a sealed crate of forgotten heirlooms, hoping to find answers. Who was Stalvan Mistmantle, and what horror did he unleash?"}},[119]={k="123",["end"]={d=147,t="You found a schedule for secret gold shipments from Elwynn Forest's mines, bound for someone called The Collector. You brought the evidence to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, who sent you to the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch to serve justice. You struck down the thief and took his ring, ending his theft from the kingdom. Yet the victory uncovered a stranger truth: the trinket was a membership ring for Stormwind's old Stonemason's Guild. The Defias Thieves siphoned wealth from the realm's mines, leaving troubling questions about what they intended to do with it."}},[120]={k="40",["end"]={d=59,t="You carried a merchant's warning about murlocs to Goldshire, but Marshal Dughan needed grim proof. At the eastern bridge, you learned guards Rolf and Malakai had vanished. Webbed footprints led you to Stone Cairn Lake, where you uncovered their grisly fate. You took the medallions from their half-eaten corpses, proving the creatures were more than a nuisance. Your report revealed a grave threat to Elwynn Forest. With defenses already stretched thin, the loss of the guards struck hard. Fresh armor from the Eastvale Logging Camp now equipped you to defend the besieged woods."}},[121]={k="94",["end"]={d=249,t="You served as Theocritus's eyes, carrying his glyphs into danger to spy on his rival. You planted his magic on an old lion statue near the Tower of Ilgalar, revealing a conflict between Morganth and the orcs. Then you hid another glyph in an empty jar at Stonewatch Keep. Through your efforts, Theocritus uncovered a terrifying truth: the warlock sought the Scythe of Elune. Rather than wait for disaster, you stormed the tower, struck Morganth down, and claimed his Pendant of Shadow. With the dark mage slain, Stormwind was spared from certain ruin."}},[123]={k="62",["end"]={d=11,t="You answered Marshal Dughan's call in Goldshire and searched the Fargodeep and Jasperlode mines, where kobolds were spreading. With local forces stretched thin, you went west to Westbrook Garrison. Deputy Rainer needed capable hands as Riverpaw gnolls overran the woods and lake shores, pressing against Elwynn Forest. You fought through their ranks and took their painted armbands as proof. Your efforts bought the defenders time and held the line against the encroaching wilds."}},[124]={k="85",["end"]={d=87,t="You began with a petty squabble between neighbors over Bernice Stonefield's missing necklace. Your search led you to hunt boars and barter a pie for the memories of a hungry boy. Billy Maclure confessed that he had lost the heirloom near the Fargodeep Mine, where Goldtooth, a hulking kobold, had seized it. You ventured underground and took the treasure from the creature. When you returned the jewelry, tears came to an old widow's eyes, and she gave you a small token of her fallen husband's luck. A piece of cherished history had found its way back to a grieving soul."}},[144]={k="2923",["end"]={d=2922,t="You brought Techbot's memory core back to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge. Brother Sarno had told you the tinkerer needed help, and Overspark mourned his mechanical assistant. When Gnomeregan fell, a jolt scrambled Techbot's positronic brain, turning the once-helpful machine into a frenzied hazard in the lost city's depths. You ended its rampage in the ruined halls and salvaged its core. Now Overspark has a vital piece of gnomish ingenuity in hand, and the chance to unravel the malfunction and restore his cherished creation."},before={a=2923,t="Brother Sarno told you how Techbot, a mechanical marvel built by the gnomes, had once been a kind and dependable helper. Its service had shown the ingenuity of its creators. Then word came that the machine had somehow broken down, its gears and logic twisted into sudden malfunction. Tinkmaster Overspark, its creator, was deeply troubled by the grim fate of his prized invention and mourned what it had become. Sarno believed there was still a chance to set things right, and held onto the hope that the broken machine could be repaired and returned to its former purpose. With that possibility in mind, you were sent to offer your assistance. Your path now led into the heart of the great dwarven mountain. You had to make your way through Ironforge's grand halls and enter Tinker Town to find Tinkmaster Overspark, where you could help salvage his ruined masterpiece."}},[145]={k="2927",["end"]={d=2962,t="Moved by Gnoarn's grief over his lost hair and Gnomeregan's fall, you traveled to Kharanos to help Ozzie Togglevolt. Seeking a cure for radiation sickness, Ozzie sent you into the infested city to gather fallout from irradiated troggs. When the sample failed, you returned to the toxic ruin and risked life and limb to extract volatile slime from the horrors in its halls. You brought back a vial of pure, concentrated ruin. Ozzie now has what he needs to test his formula, and the afflicted cling to the hope it may save them."},before={a=2927,t="You stood before a grieving gnome named Gnoarn, listening to a tale of profound loss. His sorrow was not just for the fall of a great marvel of engineering, but for the tragic ruin of his own magnificent hair, stripped away by the toxic fallout of his people's desperate defense. The radiation that seeped through the metallic halls of Gnomeregan claimed the only gnomefro in all of Azeroth, a tragedy he blamed entirely on the invasion of the filthy, relentless troggs. He shook his fist at the memory, carrying the bitter sting of a catastrophe that drove the brilliant tinkerers from their ancestral homes. Yet, in the shadow of that ruin, a faint glimmer of hope remained. A chance to undo the damage and perhaps even reclaim the lost capital still lingered in the frozen peaks. Now, you must seek out Ozzie Togglevolt and his partner Razzle in the settlement of Kharanos, where the two are tirelessly developing a method to save their irradiated city."}},[146]={k="2931",["end"]={d=2930,t="You answered Gaxim Rustfizzle's call and found Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge. After the gnomes fled Gnomeregan, they left a wealth of irreplaceable knowledge behind. Deep in the irradiated ruin, you hunted down scattered security punch cards, raising your clearance at abandoned terminals until you reached Matrix Punchograph 3005-D. There, you claimed the ultimate prize: the prismatic punch card. Returning this lost data to the surface restored a vital piece of gnomic ingenuity. Your victory stood against the tragedy that befell the gnomes' home and ensured their brilliance survived."},before={a=2931,t="Gaxim Rustfizzle asked you to answer an urgent summons from Ironforge. Gaxim Rustfizzle, a proud member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, told you the summons echoed from Ironforge, a distant mountain stronghold. Master Mechanic Castpipe sought brave souls willing to step into harm's way. Castpipe lacked the formal credentials of Gaxim's prestigious society, but his intellect remained sharp and unquestioned. Gaxim ran the calculations, and the odds showed how much the call mattered. It was too grave a situation to ignore. Now you prepare to answer. In Ironforge, Castpipe steadily gathers capable bands for a perilous, secretive undertaking. You are to join his ranks before plunging back into the treacherous depths of Gnomeregan. Your mission is to retrieve critical data from the fallen gnome city, in an operation shrouded in the highest security and importance."}},[147]={k="2925",["end"]={d=2924,t="Mathiel brought you a plea from Klockmort Spannerspan, a dear friend in need. You journeyed to Ironforge, then descended into the contaminated, maddened halls of Gnomeregan, the lost gnomish capital. Deep in the ruins, you forced open artificial extrapolators left behind during the frantic exodus and salvaged the essential artificials within. You returned with the mechanical components and delivered them to Klockmort. Those tools passed back into capable hands, and gnomish research and experimentation took a grand leap forward."},before={a=2925,t="Mathiel asked you to find his distant friend, Klockmort Spannerspan. Word of the gnome's urgent message had traveled far, but Mathiel could not leave his binding obligations to answer it himself. He yearned to rush to his companion's side, and with a heavy heart asked you to make the journey in his stead. You accepted, knowing he would remain behind and be forever grateful for your help. You traveled toward the towering dwarven gates of Ironforge, seeking Tinkertown and the gnome who needed you. There, you prepared to find Klockmort and join his desperate cause. The path ahead led into the depths of Gnomeregan, a once great marvel of gnomish engineering. Its twisting iron halls were now hopelessly contaminated, overrun by maddened gnomes and their erratic, corrupted mechanical creations. What waited within was a perilous expedition, vital to Klockmort's cause."}},[148]={k="2945A",["end"]={d=2948,t="You pulled a filth-caked ring from a dead Dark Iron dwarf and sensed magic beneath the grime. You placed it inside a Sparklematic 5200, whose clanking gears scrubbed away the dirt to reveal Ironforge's seal and three engraved initials. Tracing the letters brought you to Talvash del Kissel. He recognized the ring as his own work, left behind when Gnomeregan fell. The mystery of its presence in Dark Iron hands troubled him, but he turned his attention to his craft. For a modest fee, a bar of silver, and a moss agate, he reshaped his old creation into a finer ring for you to wear."},before={a=2945,t="You struck down the Dark Iron dwarves, their broken forms left scattered upon the unforgiving earth. Amidst the slaughter, a single prize caught your eye. Plucked from the corpse of a fallen foe, you discovered a simple band, utterly choked by thick layers of filth and caked mud. It was entirely unwearable in such a ruined state, the hardened residue clinging stubbornly to the rough surface. Yet, beneath the stifling grime, a faint luster called to you. A glimmer of precious metal hinted at fine craftsmanship, and the unmistakable glint of a hidden gem sparkled softly through the dark crust. These dwarves carried heavy secrets, and this crude trinket held mysteries of its own, locked tightly away beneath its thick shell of dirt. The true nature of this Grime-Encrusted Ring remains unknown, a stubborn mystery that resists your touch. If you are ever to make use of it, you must find something to strip the hardened residue away."}},[149]={k="2945H",["end"]={d=2950,t="You pried a grime-encrusted ring from a dead Dark Iron dwarf. After you fed a coin into the Sparklematic 5200, the shaking machine produced a shiny, gift-wrapped band sealed with the mark of Orgrimmar. That clue brought you to Nogg. He denied owning it, but saw that the Dark Irons' possession of the jewelry suggested gnomes had stolen their golem designs. Grateful for what you told him about the brewing conflict, Nogg took your silver and agate and forged a stronger lattice for the ring. The dirty salvage became a potent artifact, revealing a bitter rivalry between cunning inventors."},before={a=2945,t="You found a ring on a fallen Dark Iron dwarf, its shape hidden beneath grime. Dust still hung in the air after the battle as you searched the body and felt something small and hard among the soot stained garments. The ring was too caked with baked dirt and hardened residue to slip onto your hand. Its weight gave you pause, and beneath the filth you glimpsed the luster of precious metal and the glint of a gemstone. You turned the heavy band in your palm, wondering what it held and how it had come to be in such dark hands. Until the residue is washed away, the ring remains useless. To make use of it, you first need to find something capable of cleaning off the hardened grime."}},[150]={k="2951",["end"]={d=2952,t="Among gnomes holding out against madness, you found a strange contraption called the Sparklematic 5200. You fed it three silver coins and your encrusted prize, hoping to salvage the filthy object. The metal beast lurched and roared as its frame groaned, fighting to scour away the heavy grime. Then the racket stopped with a sudden chime. The machine opened and offered your item, neatly wrapped in a little bow. You had paid to clean it, but the pretty package concealed the result. What lies beneath the wrapping is still unknown."},before={a=2951,t="You found a small band of gnomes holding out against madness. They had huddled together as it raged just beyond their room. Nearby, a strange machine stood in the gloom, its heavy casing bearing a metal plaque that named it The Sparklematic 5200. It offered to clean the thick dirt from your equipment and restore its luster. To use it, you needed only to put three silver coins into its slot and wait while its mechanisms processed the payment. Now, amid the chaos of the survivors' refuge, you stood before the contraption with the tarnished scrap in your heavy bags. You were ready to feed your grime-covered trinkets into the machine, pay the three silver, and give it time to work. What waited ahead was a brief pause at the slot, and the hope that your belongings would emerge spotless."}},[153]={k="527",["end"]={d=550,t="You broke the human hold on Hillsbrad, striking farmers in the fields and peasants hiding in the orchards. You cut their supplies by killing Blacksmith Verringtan, then took the town registry and found the Azureload Mine, where you slaughtered the workers. You killed Magistrate Burnside and stormed the dwarven stronghold of Dun Garok, leaving Captain Ironhill dead. Back in the Undercity, you reported your victories to Varimathras. Your campaign proved to the high command that the humans could fall, and cleared the way to face the Scourge."}},[154]={k="509",["end"]={d=524,t="You gathered noxious blossoms from the fields and took them to the Undercity, where Master Apothecary Faranell added his rotting touch. With more reagents, you returned to Apothecary Lydon and helped brew a vile new plague. To test the elixir, you stole a keg of Shindigger Stout from the dwarves of Dun Garok and spiked it with the grim mixture. You left the tainted brew on a dusty rug for a group of captive human farmers. It sealed their gruesome fate, a cruel triumph for the Dark Lady."}},[155]={k="536",["end"]={d=563,t="You cleared Southshore's coast for Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, who was desperate to leave his post and too cowardly to face its dangers. The smell of the town sickened him, and he could barely stand against the murlocs and naga threatening it. You waded through the surf, killed the beasts, and carried their severed heads back to satisfy Marshal Redpath. When the order came to deal with the naga, you struck them down as well, letting Orinelle claim the glory. You delivered his report to Major Samuelson in Stormwind. The coastal threat has thinned, and Orinelle may finally win the transfer he wanted."}},[169]={k="6387",["end"]={d=6392,t="You carried a list of promising mining students from Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar over snowy peaks to Ironforge. Thorgrum Borrelson provided the wings for your journey to the Great Forge District. There, Golnir Bouldertoe received the names and carved them into a fresh batch of honorary picks. With the new tools in hand, you flew back to Loch Modan on one of Gryth Thurden's beasts. You had helped a new generation of dwarven miners begin their trade, ready to strike the region's rich ore deposits with pride."}},[171]={k="2041",["end"]={d=2040,t="You brought Shoni the Shilent an intact power supply from the Deadmines. In Stormwind, Shoni commanded an assault crew preparing to reclaim Gnomeregan from the troggs, but her gyrodrillmatic excavationators lacked the energy to pierce the city's rocky borders. Deep in the Deadmines, you recovered the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket from a functional goblin shredder and delivered the machinery back to her. Now the gnomes have the power to fuel their machines and breach the walls, and a fierce offensive to liberate their fallen home is ready."},before={a=2040,t="You joined the gnomes' fight to reclaim Gnomeregan from the vicious troggs. To aid the underground assault, you traveled to Stormwind and found Shoni the Shilent, commander of the crew. She told you her mighty gyrodrillmatic excavationators stood ready to cut through the earth, but they lacked the immense energy needed to break the subterranean stone walls around the ruined capital. Shoni sent you on a perilous mission to fuel the engines and prepare for a massive counterattack. Now you must descend into the dangerous shafts of the Deadmines and hunt for a working goblin shredder. The machine's untouched power source could give the great drills the strength to pierce Gnomeregan's rocky perimeter. If you can dismantle the shredder and secure that power, the gnomish forces can pour through the breach and take back their home."}},[174]={k="224",["end"]={d=217,t="You held Loch Modan's fragile front while King Magni's soldiers fought on distant battlefields. Troggs threatened to overwhelm Ironforge, and you thinned the Stonesplinter forces to buy the mountaineers time. When you learned that no reinforcements would come, you stood against the swarm. You struck at its heart, killing Chieftain Grawmug and his towering guards, Gnasher and Brawler. With their leaders gone, the invasion collapsed, and the dwarven lands were safe."}},[176]={k="298",["end"]={d=309,t="You carried a simple request for blastpowder from Prospector Ironband to Thelsamar, then to Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge. Earlier shipments had vanished without a trace. When you hurried back to check the latest delivery, you found the porters under attack by their own companion. The missing powder had not vanished by chance: Dark Iron sympathizers like Saean had infiltrated the crew to steal supplies. You drove off the ambushers, guarded Miran on the road, and brought the remaining barrels safely to the excavation. Ironband had his powder, but traitors still hid among the dwarves."}},[178]={k="250",["end"]={d=283,t="You stopped a deadly plot at the Stonewrought Dam. After finding strange powder nearby, you recognized the threat and braved the road to Dun Modr. There, an explosives expert identified it as volatile Seaforium. You hunted venomous spiders, gathered tears from crocolisks, and wrested rare crystals from ogres to prepare a neutralizing mixture. Then you dove to the base of the dam and poured the compound into a planted keg just before it could detonate. The explosives fizzled, the massive stone structure held firm, and the Dark Iron insurgents' devastating strike was thwarted. The Stonewrought Dam remains safe."}},[182]={k="752",["end"]={d=776,t="You earned your place among your people through service, vision, and the hunt. After fetching water for Greatmother Hawkwind, you caught the Chief's eye. He sent you to Baine Bloodhoof, who passed you to Zarlman Two-Moons. From well stones and ambercorn, you brewed the Water of the Seers, drank before the fire, and followed a vision to Red Rocks. There, the Ancestral Spirits blessed you and granted you entrance to Thunder Bluff. Before Cairne Bloodhoof, you tracked the mighty kodo Arra'chea across Mulgore and claimed its horn. Your hunt gave the tribe meat and secured your honored place among them."},mid={d=767,t="You carried Greatmother Hawkwind's water pitcher from the well to Chief Hawkwind. To spare her weary legs, you had sought her out by the quiet well outside Camp Narache. Impressed by your dedication to the tribe, Chief Hawkwind entrusted you with his carved totem and sent you down the dusty road to Bloodhoof Village. Baine Bloodhoof recognized the mark of his friend and welcomed you to continue your trials. He sent you to Zarlman Two-Moons, the spiritual leader, who sensed your arrival before you spoke. You had traveled far to prove your worth to the distant elders of Thunder Bluff. What truths the holy land would reveal to your eyes remained unknown."}},[183]={k="6365",["end"]={d=6386,t="You carried Zargh's prime cuts of meat to Devrak at the Crossroads, then flew by wind rider to Orgrimmar. There, you gave the gift to Innkeeper Gryshka, whose favor you won with the fine steaks. She gave you a letter of gratitude. With Doras's help, you rode the swift winds back to the Barrens and put her reply in Zargh's hands. He was thrilled by her warm response. Your deliveries had kindled an unexpected romance in a harsh land, forging a lasting connection from a humble offering."}},[184]={k="5726",["end"]={d=5730,t="You carried a cultist's insignia from Skull Rock to prove your worth to Thrall. At his command, you took the mark into the Cleft of Shadow and deceived Neeru Fireblade by posing as a loyal servant of the Burning Blade. Then you descended into Ragefire Chasm and assassinated Bazzalan and Jergosh, crippling the cult's leadership beneath the city. Neeru confessed, unaware of your deception, that the Shadow Council was shifting its dark work into the Barrens and Ashenvale. You rooted out Orgrimmar's immediate threat and armed the Warchief with vital intelligence about the rot spreading through his lands."},before={a=5728,t="You earned Thrall's trust when no one else could be relied on. He suspected a treacherous infection within his own city, one he could not purge openly without causing it to spread. He sent you into Skull Rock to expose the Burning Blade, and you returned with a lieutenant's insignia. With it, you descended into the Cleft of Shadow and deceived the warlock who secretly leads the cult. He believed you were one of his own and revealed the names of his most valued allies. The trap was set. Thrall has directed you into the fiery depths of Ragefire Chasm to sever the cult's power. You must find Bazzalan, the satyr, and the warlock leader of the Searing Blade, and execute them. Strike without letting Neeru discover your true loyalties, and keep your identity as a dedicated member of his twisted brotherhood."}},[185]={k="1431",["end"]={d=1436,t="You heard Craven Drok describe the Warchief's careful diplomacy, then sought Keldran in his hovel. Keldran revealed a grim political reality: the Alliance was pushing deeper into Kalimdor, and any lingering demonic presence could be mistaken for a renewed pact between the Horde and the Burning Legion. Far to the west in Desolace, you found Takata Steelblade struggling against a rampant demon infestation. Purging the corruption helped the native centaur and did more than aid them indirectly. It silenced damning rumors before they could begin, proving to a wary world that the Horde's dark history remained buried."}},[187]={k="5722",["end"]={d=5724,t="You searched Ragefire Chasm in Orgrimmar for Maur Grimtotem, sent there by Rahauro. Magatha believed her servant had found something peculiar before he vanished. Deep underground, you found his battered corpse, beaten to death by savage troggs. Maur still clutched a satchel, guarding his discovery to his dying breath. You took the Grimtotem Satchel from his lifeless grasp and carried it safely to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff. Whatever Maur unearthed now rested in the hands of the Grimtotem clan."},before={a=5722,t="You learned that Maur Grimtotem had vanished beneath Orgrimmar. Rahauro told you the servant had been sent into Ragefire Chasm to parley with the brutish troggs below the city. There, Maur found something unusual, a secret he meant to bring back to Magatha. The earth swallowed him, and neither Maur nor his prize returned to the surface. You accepted the burden of uncovering his fate. The trail leads down into sweltering volcanic caverns, where hostile tunnels may have consumed him. Whatever strange artifact or forbidden knowledge he uncovered must be reclaimed from heat and ash. You must descend into the deepest reaches of the city, brave the troggs, and pull Maur's corpse from the chasm. Any trace of his discovery must be recovered with it."}},[189]={k="120",["end"]={d=146,t="You carried Magistrate Solomon's desperate pleas for aid from Lakeshire to Stormwind, then Westfall, and finally Duskwood. The Stormwind Army's General Marcus Jonathan offered only vague promises, while Gryan Stoutmantle's militia fought its own lonely war in Westfall. On Duskwood's roads, Lord Ello Ebonlocke refused to sacrifice his Night Watch. Every leader revealed the same bitter truth: Stormwind had abandoned its people to fend for themselves. Solomon now understands that treachery has taken root in the capital, leaving the outer regions defenseless."}},[202]={k="421",["end"]={d=99,t="To earn Dalar Dawnweaver's trust, you struck down the Moonrage Whitescalps stalking Silverpine Forest. You sought the roots of Arugal's reckless sorcery, taking a forgotten remedy from an abandoned farm and enchanted shackles from the wandering beasts. You secured Deep Elem Mine for the Forsaken by severing Grimson the Pale's head. In Pyrewood Village, you gathered twisted bindings from cursed peasants who changed from men into savage worgen at nightfall. Now Dawnweaver holds the knowledge to undo Arugal's magic, clearing the way for the Dark Lady to conquer the forest."}},[203]={k="428",["end"]={d=425,t="You searched northern Silverpine for two missing Deathstalkers and found Rane and Quinn Yorick at a farm. Quinn lay severely wounded after a ghoul attacked him, so you hunted worgs for their discolored hearts. You brought the hearts to the Sepulcher and returned with a healing potion from Apothecary Renferrel. After Quinn took the medicine, you cornered Ivar the Foul in a nearby barn and struck him down. With the monster slain and its head delivered as proof, the Deathstalkers were safe, their survival ensured."}},[204]={k="435",["end"]={d=1358,t="You led Deathstalker Erland safely past Silverpine Forest's ravenous wolves to Rane Yorick. You carried their urgent report on the Scourge to High Executor Hadrec, then Apothecary Renferrel summoned you. He had found a baffling, deadly toxin in the wolves' hearts. You took his samples to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity, and she quickly saw the discovery's dark potential. She sent you across the sea with the tainted flesh for Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads. Now this strange Lordaeron poison rests in his hands, ready to advance the Forsaken's deadly knowledge."}},[205]={k="437",["end"]={d=442,t="You destroyed Nightlash, a banshee, at the Dead Fields, then traced the Decrepit Ferry's stolen corpses across Lordamere Lake to Fenris Isle. After you brought the rot hides' tainted blood to the Undercity, you uncovered Thule Ravenclaw, the treacherous mage allied with the Scourge behind the harvest. Armed with counter-magics, you stormed his island stronghold and severed his head. His destruction sent arcane power surging for miles. The corpse trade has been halted, and your blow has weakened the Lich King's grasp on these plagued lands."},mid={d=443,t="You struck at the rot hide gnolls in the Dead Fields and destroyed the banshee Nightlash, breaking the Scourge's momentum. The danger ran deeper than their camp. At the Decrepit Ferry, you found a ruined boat piled with stolen corpses bound for Fenris Isle across Lordamere Lake. An engraved ring on a recently slain woman confirmed the dead had been dragged from Tirisfal's mass graves. You crossed to the island seeking the architect of this harvest and extracted the foul ichor coursing through the gnolls' veins. Now Apothecary Renferrel studies the vile fluid at the Sepulcher, hoping to find a weakness and discover who truly commands the rot hides from the shadows."}},[206]={k="477",["end"]={d=480,t="You followed the Dalaran wizards' shipments to a camp north of Pyrewood Village and found old maps and a magical pendant. Shadow Priest Allister sent it to Dalar Dawnweaver for study, and he uncovered the Kirin Tor's plan to channel power through the pendants and awaken a dormant ley energy node within Ambermill. You fought the town's defenders and took their artifacts to hinder the ritual. Then you struck down the archmage guiding the spellwork and claimed his staff. The magic faded, silencing the ley node and dealing a heavy blow to the human forces."}},[208]={k="6421",["end"]={d=6481,t="You followed the kobolds' frantic mining of Resonite crystals deep into Boulderslide Ravine and brought samples to Mor'rogal. They had dug too deep, uncovering Goggeroc, a slumbering Earthen. The Titans had forged these ancient beings to shape the world, and Goggeroc's raw power could not go unchecked. With an enchanted crystal, you shattered his prison and struck down the weakened giant. The danger was gone, and Goggeroc's primordial wrath could no longer threaten Stonetalon or all of Kalimdor."}},[211]={k="1077",["end"]={d=1084,t="You used Gaxim Rustfizzle's explosives to infiltrate the Venture Co. lumber mill. The sabotage let you steal their engineering plans and confidential letters, striking hard at their deforesting efforts. When you delivered the secrets to Kaela Shadowspear, you learned the horror of the goblins' retreat: they had set the Vale ablaze and roused enraged spirits of flame and stone, which you were forced to strike down. Their destructive weapons had corrupted even the noble treants. You gathered shrapnel from the wounded ancients, giving the Sentinels the means to understand the strange corruption plaguing the forest."}},[212]={k="1483",["end"]={d=1096,t="You found Ziz Fizziks, a disgruntled goblin in Windshear Crag, angry that the Venture Company had replaced him with Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle, a gnome. To claim a place in the Tinkers' Union, you stole blueprints for a massive woodcutting machine and delivered them to Sputtervalve in Ratchet. The trade princes demanded more than corporate espionage: they wanted the gnome dead. You returned to the crag and climbed high above the lake to face Gerenzo, a twisted engineer with mechanical limbs grafted to his rotting flesh. Now he lay dead, a brutal message delivered, while Ziz hoped his new masters would welcome him home."}},[220]={k="343",["end"]={d=346,t="You went looking for a book on metallurgy for Brother Kristoff, but The Stresses of Iron was not easy to retrieve. Stormwind's librarian sent you to Northshire Abbey, where Brother Paxton had stopped copying because his ink had run dry. You sought rare Rethban ore to brew more ink, but in Lakeshire the supplier was busy preparing for orc attacks. You descended into the gnoll-infested Rethban Caverns and mined the stone yourself, then brought the raw ore to the abbey. Brother Paxton finished his copy, and Brother Kristoff received the original tome, ready to share its wisdom."}},[221]={k="3765",["end"]={d=1275,t="Argos Nightwhisper sent you from Stormwind across the sea to aid his brother in Auberdine. There, Gershala feared that the blood elves' meddling with demonic magic would twist them into monsters. To learn the truth of their impending fate, you hunted the corrupted creatures haunting Ashenvale's coast. You descended into Blackfathom Deeps and claimed the corrupted remains of naga and satyr alike. With those grim trophies delivered, Gershala began his study, seeking answers that might spare Azeroth from another monstrous threat."},before={a=1275,t="Argos Nightwhisper sent you from Stormwind to Darkshore. Amid Stormwind's bustle, you heard his plea for an experienced druid to undertake an epic journey. In the coastal town of Auberdine, you met his brother, Gershala Nightwhisper, who feared the blood elves' reckless meddling with demonic magic. He worried they would suffer the same twisted, monstrous deformation that long ago befell the naga and satyrs of Kalimdor. To uncover the dark path the elves were walking and prevent the birth of another vile race, Gershala asked you to retrieve the brain stems of those corrupted beings for his studies. Now a long road leads to the shores of Ashenvale, where satyr and naga await in the treacherous depths of Blackfathom Deeps."}},[222]={k="337",["end"]={d=542,t="You lifted a muddy, scratched history book from the dirt and returned it to Stormwind's shelves. Trusting your dedication, the library sent you north to salvage more. The old kingdom of Alterac lay in ruins after the great war, its vast collection of tomes left to the ogres squatting in the rubble. You traveled to Southshore, then braved Alterac's crumbling walls. There, you tore the stolen books from the beasts' grasp and secured a worn leather text of ancient troll lore. In a world scarred by conflict, you ensured the wisdom of the past would survive."}},[265]={k="4495",["end"]={d=3522,t="Dirania Silvershine feared for her missing friend, and you searched the shadowed depths of the northern cave. There, you found Iverron succumbing to Githyiss the Vile's virulent poison. Racing against his fading life, you gathered Hyacinth mushrooms, Moonpetal lilies, and Webwood ichor from the spiders that had bitten him. You hurried back through the darkness and delivered Dirania's volatile antidote before time ran out. The serum purged the venom from his veins, and you spared a foolish explorer a wretched death. Swift action had snatched Iverron's life back from the brink."}},[266]={k="916",mid={d=921,t="You entered Shadowglen to learn why the forest's beasts had changed. Guided by Gilshalan Windwalker, you braved Shadowthread Cave and took toxic venom and an unhatched egg from its giant webwood spiders. The specimens were bound for Darnassus, where they could reveal the new world tree's influence. You climbed to the heights of Aldrassil and answered Tenaron Stormgrip's summons. He spoke of a changed people, victory at Mount Hyjal, and ancient Nordrassil, now a pale shadow of its former glory. At his behest, you drew sacred water from the moonwell. The full story of the battle's aftermath remained unclear, and you still did not know what awaited within the greater expanse of Teldrassil."},["end"]={d=935,t="You began by harvesting venom and an unhatched egg from giant webwood spiders, revealing mutations caused by the new world tree. The tragic history of your people drew you between Teldrassil's moonwells, where you gathered their sacred waters in filled vessels. With each vessel, you learned the bitter truth: planted without the blessings of Nozdormu and Alexstrasza, the great tree was fundamentally flawed and drove native beasts to madness. You delivered the combined waters to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus. Now he must bear the weight of his arrogant creation and hope the waters can cure its spreading corruption."}},[267]={k="997",["end"]={d=2499,t="You brought rare earth to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth, where angry, erratic timberlings had stirred trouble. You gathered their seeds and sought answers from Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus. He found that deep corruption had tainted the elementals. At Wellspring Lake, you purged the twisted creatures and tore away the mossy tumors poisoning them. The source lay hidden at Lake Al'Ameth, inside a southern cave. There, a gargantuan tumor had corrupted Oakenscowl, a noble leader among his kind. You struck down Oakenscowl and secured the massive blight. Now Denalan can study the disease threatening Teldrassil and hope to save its natural order."}},[270]={k="488",["end"]={d=489,t="You served Zenn Foulhoof, the satyr, after hidden promises lured you in. You slaughtered Teldrassil's creatures for his reagents, then learned he had made a gullible pawn of you. Your bloodshed angered the Council of the Forest, who demanded you atone for defiling their woods. To regain their trust, you gathered corrupted fel cones and offered them to Zenn as an innocent treat. He swallowed the tainted gift without hesitation. Your trickery answered his own, restoring your honor and making him suffer for his deceit."}},[271]={k="4542",["end"]={d=5064,t="You carried Brave Moonhorn's warning of worsening attacks to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post. After learning a caravan had been massacred, you rode north and struck down the centaur assailants in retribution. A separate, shadowy threat also loomed over the bluffs. Reports of strange outsiders led you up Darkcloud Pinnacle, where you stole hidden missives from the Grimtotem Clan. The documents you brought back revealed a sweeping conspiracy. Now its defenders hold that chilling revelation, and Freewind Post must brace for the danger ahead."}},[272]={k="1149",["end"]={d=1394,t="You journeyed into the unknown to prove your spirit to Dorn Plainstalker, then waded through the Roguefeather Den and felled Grenka Bloodscreech. In Thousand Needles, you shattered the ancient elemental Rok'Alim. Flesh and bone were only half a champion's measure, so you braved Dor'danil's slayers to claim the Legacy of the Aspects for Braug Dimspirit. At last, you journeyed to Lordaeron City to satisfy the skeptical scholar Parqual Fintallas. Brutal combat and quiet study tested your body, mind, and spirit, and found you unbreakable. You stand now as a truly enlightened warrior."},mid={d=1154,t="You sought Dorn Plainstalker's trial of spirit, body, and mind. You began with a blind leap into the unknown, relying on faith to carry you through adversity. Then you pushed your flesh to its limits. In a harpy den, you provoked and killed Grenka Bloodscreech, then hunted Rok'Alim, an ancient elemental in Thousand Needles. After proving your endurance and strength, you traveled north to find Braug Dimspirit. He dismissed your past battles as childish and commanded you to brave the haunted depths of Dor'danil, where dead druids guarded a heavy tome. You returned with the book, but your trial of intellect still remains. What ancient secrets will Braug demand you recall?"}},[273]={k="4821",["end"]={d=5088,t="You sought an alien egg in the serpent dens of Thousand Needles, and its retrieval revealed that Arikara, a legendary spirit of vengeance, had awakened. You harvested rare agave from the Boiling Pool and delivered it to Magatha Grimtotem in Thunder Bluff. With her enchanted powder, you ignited a sacred flame atop the Darkcloud Pinnacle and drew the beast into battle. You struck Arikara down, but Motega Firemane's praise could not settle the doubt. The claim that Arikara had hunted Cairne Bloodhoof left him unsettled. The immediate threat was gone, but the mystery endured."}},[274]={k="1100",["end"]={d=1101,t="You carried a battered journal from a fallen dwarf to Falfindel Waywarder. Its worn pages told of the bitter ends of Henrig Lonebrow and Heralath. When you learned Charlga Razorflank was responsible, you gathered allies and entered the Kraul. Deep among its thorns, you fought your way to the crone and struck her down. You took her medallion as proof. Researchers can now investigate the corruption blighting Agamaggan's resting grounds in safety, though they fear deeper treachery lies behind the rot."},before={a=1101,t="Henrig Lonebrow's journal brought you to Falfindel Waywarder. You found it in the wilderness, taken from the cold grip of the deceased dwarf, then carried its bleak pages to Falfindel for guidance. The grim accounts told of the bitter ends met by the brave Lonebrow and poor Heralath. Falfindel would not let their valiant sacrifices fade into nothing. He learned that Charlga Razorflank, a wicked crone, had guided them to their untimely doom. The threat mounted, and there was no time to send word to distant Darnassus for aid. Vengeance fell to you. Now you needed to gather a loyal party and infiltrate the dark, tangled depths of the Kraul. Your path led to the crone where she dwelled: slay her, then claim Razorflank's Medallion as proof of her demise."}},[281]={k="6361",["end"]={d=6364,t="You carried a bundle of raw pelts from the Crossroads to Thunder Bluff, soaring high above the Barrens on a wind rider. There, Ahanu made fine leather goods from the hides. You flew back and delivered the finished wares to Jahan Hawkwing. The errand strengthened a vital trade link between the growing settlements. By bringing the durable leathers to the Crossroads, you equipped countless travelers flocking to the outpost with what they needed to survive in unforgiving territory."}},[282]={k="1061",["end"]={d=1086,t="The Venture Company's logging in the Stonetalon Mountains drew cries of pain from the spirits. You answered with violence, but bloodshed alone could not stop them. In Thunder Bluff, Magatha Grimtotem directed you toward the Forsaken's dark arts. At distant Tarren Mill, you took stolen innocent blood from Syndicate mages for Apothecary Lydon to brew into a devastating toxin. With Zamah's refined poison, you infiltrated the goblin camps and planted it at their hidden flying machine airport. The brew now spreads toward their headquarters, crippling the plunderers and securing a ruthless victory for the land."},mid={d=1064,t="You found Seereth Stonebreak in the Stonetalon Mountains, where the land's cries had led you. The shaman told you the Venture Company goblins were felling forests, driving local spirits mad with pain and rage. At her call, you killed timber workers in Windshear Crag, showing the Horde's resolve. Yet brute force could not soothe the spirits. Seereth sent you to the heights of Thunder Bluff to consult the elder Magatha Grimtotem. Magatha believed the land must first be cleansed of its disease, and guided you to Apothecary Zamah in the shadowy Pools of Vision. What unnatural remedies might the Forsaken emissary unleash to mend the broken earth remained unknown."}},[283]={k="1195",["end"]={d=1197,t="You traveled far into Ashenvale Forest and secured a small phial from the dryads. You filled it with water from a sacred moonwell, then carried the precious fluid south to Freewind Post in the Thousand Needles. There, you learned its magic could pierce the fiery defenses guarding a treasure. You fought the savage Galak centaur in Splithoof Hold and used the water to briefly smother the undying fires, taking a revered relic. When you delivered the ancient hoof to Rau Cliffrunner, its pulsing power revealed an unknown force that would finally unravel the hidden origins of their entire race."}},[285]={k="363",["end"]={d=383,t="You woke in Deathknell's crypt, freed from the Lich King's iron will. Guided by Undertaker Mordo and Shadow Priest Sarvis, you struck down the mindless undead haunting your new home and gathered supplies to survive. You cleared a gold mine infested with spiders, then turned against the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. After intercepting their messenger, you took a vital map to Executor Zygand in Brill. The map revealed the locations of the crusade's field commanders to the Forsaken, and your people now stand ready to cut down those zealous foes' leadership."}},[286]={k="367",["end"]={d=492,t="You answered Lady Sylvanas's call to help the Royal Apothecary Society forge a disease deadly enough to break Arthas and his Scourge. In Brill, you aided Apothecary Johaan, gathering darkhound blood, murloc scales, and venom from vicious night web spiders to perfect the brew. Once the concoction was complete and boiling, you descended into the cellar of the Gallows End Tavern to test it on a captured dwarven mountaineer. He drank deeply to quench his thirst, facing the doom that awaited him and the terrifying future the Dark Lady plans for all of Azeroth."}},[288]={k="358",["end"]={d=411,t="You earned Magistrate Sevren's trust by killing the Rot Hide gnolls who gathered corpses for the Scourge. He sent you to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity, who asked you to steal a spellbook from a lone lich on Brightwater Lake. The lich was Gunther Arcanus, once a mage of the Kirin Tor. After you returned the enchanted book and destroyed the Scourge agent Lillith Nefara, Gunther understood that other undead had escaped the Lich King's grasp. He gave you a Nether Gem, ending his isolation and placing his formidable necromantic knowledge in Forsaken hands."}},[289]={k="427",["end"]={d=372,t="You used the intercepted documents to break the Scarlet Crusade across Tirisfal Glades. Executor Zygand pointed you toward its footholds. You culled the warriors in the tower beyond the Solliden Farmstead, then hunted their officers. At a ruined tower, you killed Captain Perrine and his zealots. Near the Balnir Farmstead, you struck down Captain Vachon. You marched past Faol's Rest to kill the ruthless Captain Melrache. With its leaders gone, the crusade's advance was halted. The Dark Lady was pleased by your bloodshed, and the Forsaken stood one step closer to their ultimate revenge against Arthas."}},[292]={k="6321",["end"]={d=6324,t="You carried Deathguard Podrig's requisition from the Sepulcher through the gloom to the Undercity. There, you found weapons dealer Gordon Wendham and gave him the request. He packed a heavy crate of armaments, and you flew it back to the remote outpost in Silverpine. The Deathguards now stand ready with fresh steel to fend off the Scourge lurking in the woods, their grim duty to the Dark Lady better supplied as shadows close in."}},[295]={k="6981A",["end"]={d=3370,t="You found a brilliant green crystal with smoky depths and brought it to Ratchet for answers. Falla Sagewind recognized it as the pure essence of the Emerald Dream, but recoiled from the dark visions within. She urged you to carry the nightmare-tainted stone to Darnassus. There, you entrusted it to Mathrengyl Bearwalker. When he peered into the glass, the grim truth shook him. He locked the danger away and warned that the realm of nature slumbers in unseen peril. You left the Cenarion druids with a dark secret, and they alone must face whatever corruption now stirs beneath the dream."},before={a=6981,t="You uncovered a shard of brilliant green crystal, completely solid to the touch. Yet, just beneath its smooth surface, shadows that looked exactly like thick smoke swirled and shifted continuously. Your eyes were drawn deep into the heart of the stone, mesmerized by the silent, unnatural movement trapped inside. A strange fascination took hold of your mind, making it nearly impossible to look away from the emerald depths. However, even as you stared, a creeping sense of dread washed over you. The longer you held the heavy crystal, the more certain you became that there was something deeply and fundamentally disturbing about its very nature. The origin of the corrupt relic remained a complete mystery, but ignoring its existence was simply not an option. Needing answers, you turned your attention toward the arid shores to the east. You set out to see if anyone in Ratchet can tell you more about this strange shard."}},[296]={k="6981H",["end"]={d=3369,t="You found a vibrant green crystal with smoke swirling beneath its solid shell. Disturbed by its unnatural aura, you carried the unsettling stone to Falla Sagewind in Ratchet. She recognized the artifact as a pure piece of the Emerald Dream, yet saw only a horrifying nightmare trapped inside. Unwilling to keep it, she sent you far away to Thunder Bluff. There, you gave the burden to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise. He warned you to forget the matter, but his unease proved the worst. You surrendered the shard, but a grim truth remains: corruption infects the Emerald Dream."},before={a=6981,t="You discovered a brilliant green shard, a stone unlike any you had ever seen. Though its crystalline surface felt completely solid and unyielding in your hands, a restless energy seemed trapped within. When you looked closely, it was as if thick, dark smoke swirled continually just beneath the surface, shifting and churning with a life of its own. You found yourself utterly captivated, unable to pull your gaze away from the hypnotic depths of the crystal. Yet, beneath that strange fascination, a profound sense of unease washed over you. A creeping dread whispered in your mind, warning you that there was something fundamentally and deeply disturbing about the object you now carried. It was not a natural thing, and the heavy burden of its dark presence weighed upon you. Seeking answers to ease your troubled thoughts, you turn your steps toward the coast. Now, you set out for Ratchet, seeking anyone who might tell you more about this strange shard."}},[298]={k="6181",["end"]={d=6285,t="You brought the defenders of Sentinel Hill's plea to Stormwind, flying above the forests on a gryphon. They needed armor for an outpost the kingdom had nearly forgotten. In the city, you gathered heavy crates of steel and leather, then carried them back through the clouds. The embattled soldiers received the protection they needed to hold the line. Through this vital trade, you forged a lasting link across the open skies, where help was never more than a flight away."}},[300]={k="92742",["end"]={d=92819,t="You traced Westfall's poisoned farmlands to tainted wells and searched the shoreline for its source. The local mines offered no answers, but suspicious supplies led you into the abandoned Deadmines. In Stormwind, you gathered dynamite and a remote detonator from SI:7, then returned to plant the bomb in a hidden forge. The blast collapsed its machinery and stopped the toxins. Behind the devastation lay no mere bandit scheme: Stormwind's endless hunger for war had sacrificed the very earth and citizens the kingdom was meant to defend."},mid={d=92748,t="You drew water from the wells at the Jansen Stead and Molsen Farm to trace the poison plaguing Westfall. You searched the shore for murloc gills and found the corruption had not reached the sea. Toxic metals in the well samples led you to strike down Defias laborers in the Jangolode Mine and Gold Coast Quarry, but the poison came from elsewhere. In abandoned Moonbrook, heavy industrial supplies revealed a massive hidden operation. You went to the Dwarven District of Stormwind to find an engineer whose explosives might shatter the machinery choking the land. What industry churned in the black depths of the Deadmines, and whose hands guided its toxic work, remained unknown."}},[301]={k="136",["end"]={d=140,t="After Captain Sanders died, the map he left behind led you on a long hunt across Westfall. You found his sandy footlocker by a rusted anchor on the western coast and took a clue from a scurrying crab. Eastward up the bluffs, a ruined chimney hid the next piece in a broken barrel. North at a lone windmill, you pulled a whiskey-soaked note from an empty jug. Guided to the shore, you swam west to an island and forced open his locked chest. Captain Sanders may rest in a watery grave, but you claimed his fortune."}},[310]={k="473",["end"]={d=474,t="You answered Valstag Ironjaw's summons and faced Captain Stoutfist as the Dragonmaw clan gathered strength. Decimated in the Second War, the orcs rallied under Chieftain Nek'rosh, driven by revenge. You entered their camp for their war banners, then learned they planned to lay siege to Menethil Harbor. Fire consumed their catapults, and in the chaos you claimed Nek'rosh's head. With their leader and siege engines destroyed, the Dragonmaw's resurgence was broken, the harbor was safe, and you had won Ironforge's favor."}},[311]={k="288",["end"]={d=293,t="You met the Third Fleet's sole survivor, drowning his memories. First Mate Fitzsimmons told you dragonfire had doomed his ships and a dark treasure had bound his fallen crew. You waded through the wreckage, put his restless shipmates to the sword, and struck down Captain Halyndor. In the sunken ruins, you recovered the relic that tormented them: an Eye of Paleth. Glorin Steelbrow could not purge its malice, so you carried the tainted orb to Stormwind. Archbishop Benedictus cleansed its deep sorrow, lifting the curse and allowing Kul Tiras's dead sailors to find peace."}},[312]={k="303",["end"]={d=378,t="You drove the Dark Iron dwarves back from the Thandol Span and Dun Modr before the reserves arrived. You broke their encampment and gave King Magni's loyal soldiers a chance to fight. Holding the territory was not enough. You learned that Kam Deepfury had orchestrated the assault that killed Longbraid's brother, then tracked him to his cell in the Stormwind Stockade. You killed Kam Deepfury, bypassing his political shielding to carry out a swift execution. His death brought solace to the mourning families, and vengeance reached the one who had ordered the assault."},before={a=378,t="Dun Modr lay in ruins as the Alliance fought in distant lands. The Dark Iron Dwarves had crippled the Thandol Span, striking the home front with ruthless precision. At Motley Garmason's call, you fought back, striking down their tunnelers and saboteurs and pressing hard enough to halt their advance while you hoped the reserves would arrive. Your courage showed your loyalty to King Magni. But the fighting had a deeper cause. Garmason revealed that intelligence gathered by Roggo pointed to a conspirator behind the destruction of the Thandol Span, the act that cost Longbraid his kin. Kam Deepfury, the architect of that ruin, was protected by political maneuvering and held in the Stormwind Stockade. Now you march to the capital, tasked with breaching the prison walls and returning with Kam Deepfury's head."}},[314]={k="631",["end"]={d=634,t="You found Ebenezer Rustlocke dead at the Thandol Span, clutching orders that exposed a Dark Iron plot. Kam Deepfury planned to destroy the last crossing and sever the north from Khaz Modan. You destroyed the hidden explosives stockpile before it could be triggered, keeping the route open. In the Arathi Highlands, you sought reinforcements from Captain Nials, but found another disaster. Stromgarde had fallen, and the soldiers at Refuge Pointe were trapped in their own desperate struggle. The bridge remained whole, while Longbraid and his dwarves faced the fight at Dun Modr alone."}},[316]={k="92460A",["end"]={d=92472,t="You came of age among the shen'dorei in Thendal Village, carrying an ancestral relic from Rorian the Dayseeker. You helped restore the grove's balance by culling wild vuldren and calming wind sprites driven to violence by the Al'Aketh cult. After exposing the cultists, you faced Elder Aetheen of the Gales' test: a battle against Urs'anah, the vicious ursera matriarch. You prevailed, left the grove, and traveled south to Shen'dar Village. Before Constable Aonda, you proved you were no fledgling, but a defender ready to face the rising storm of the Al'Aketh."},mid={d=92465,t="You came to Thendal Village to mark your coming of age among the shen'dorei. Beneath the greatfather tree, Rorian the Dayseeker gave you an ancestral relic, a token of your people's resilience. You began by thinning the local vuldren to protect the grove's balance, but their restless nature pointed to deeper magical trouble. At the ancient standing stones, Yala Windwatcher uncovered the cause: the Al'Aketh cult. You had to shed the blood of your own kin as you dispersed the corrupted wind sprites and struck down the zealots. You have driven the cultists back for now. What first stirred them to agitate the winds remains unknown."}},[317]={k="92460H",["end"]={d=92472,t="You came of age in Thendal Village, where Rorian the Dayseeker gave you your relic. You culled the restless vuldren and battled through the winds to strike down the Al'Aketh cultists in the grove. After warning the elders of the threat, you proved your strength to Aetheen of the Gales by slaying the savage matriarch Urs'anah. Then you left the village's safety and journeyed south. In Shen'dar Village, you presented yourself to Constable Aonda, ready to use your proven might against the cult's growing darkness."},mid={d=92465,t="You reached Thendal Village eager to prove yourself, and Rorian the Dayseeker gave you a sacred relic at the greatfather tree. It bound you to the history of the shen'dorei and the winds of Zephras. Peace in Thendal Grove proved fragile. You culled the local vuldren, docile creatures driven to unpredictable behavior by imbalanced magic. When simple wind sprites near the standing stones grew agitated, Rorian sent you to Yala Windwatcher. She found that the Al'Aketh cult had infiltrated the island and stirred the air to violence. You struck down your corrupted kin and dispersed the roiling winds, protecting your home. The immediate chaos has passed, but the cult's true motives in the grove remain unknown."}},[10]={k="691",["end"]={d=697,t="You entered the untamed Arathi Highlands to aid Kryten and Skuerto, claiming vital reagents from Witherbark trolls and recovering a stolen wand from the ogre Kor'gresh. Within Stromgarde's shattered walls, you seized a shamanic gem and awakened the Tower of Arathor's dormant defenses. They parted a sea of Boulderfist ogres just enough for you to recover Trelane's most prized artifacts. You returned those ancient relics to Archmage Malin in Stormwind. Your bloodshed in the highlands pulled a master's legacy back from the brink of ruin and brought the mages' dangerous mission to a close."}},[15]={k="665",["end"]={d=667,t="You guarded Professor Phizzlethorpe during an ambush, powering gnomish goggles that let you gather calcified elven gems from the sea floor. You brought the sunken treasure to Captain Shakes O'Breen, carried a sample south to Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay, then returned to the Arathi coast with secret orders. There, Daggerspine naga rose from the waves to slaughter the stranded pirates. You manned the ship's cannon and drove the attackers back into the deep. O'Breen and his crew will sail home on the rising tide, alive because of you."}},[72]={k="1361",["end"]={d=1366,t="You answered Regthar Deathgate's call in the Barrens and marched into Desolace. Felgur Twocuts warned that the warring centaur clans might unite against the Horde. You struck fast to prevent that, assassinating Khan Dez'hepah and throwing the Kolkar into chaos. You also swept across the dry plains, taking ears from centaurs to bleed their numbers. You broke their resolve, and the surviving clans now whisper your name in terror as the Horde's banner casts its deadly shadow over their ancestral plains."}},[87]={k="317",["end"]={d=320,t="You gathered meat and thick furs from the frozen fields for Pilot Bellowfiz's siege mission, then carried them to Steelgrill's Depot. His tank was nearly provisioned, but the cold demanded fuel that could warm the pilot and power his steam engine. At Brewnall Village, you culled the encroaching beasts of the snow so Rejold Barleybrew could brew in peace. You brought a heavy cask of his famous Evershine to Pilot Bellowfiz, and Jetsteam was ready for whatever danger the Siege Brigade pointed it toward."}},[122]={k="106",["end"]={d=114,t="You carried letters between two feuding farming families, choosing young love over old grudges. You sought an elder's wisdom and an alchemist's craft, then faced the murlocs of Crystal Lake to gather their strange kelp. Back in Goldshire, you secured a potion of invisibility and placed it in Maybell's hands. The lovers can now steal a few moments together in the shadows, while the rivalry between their households remains unbroken. Your efforts gave their devotion room to flourish, even as the feud endures."}},[160]={k="533",["end"]={d=508,t="You searched the Syndicate camps and found Gol'dir, the captive expedition leader, suffering under his human jailers. Aliden Perenolde meant to enslave the orcs as his mentor Blackmoore once had, and that ambition was twisted. You brought swift justice to Aliden Perenolde at his manor by the lake, killing the so-called lord. You spared his terrified mistress, Elysa, and took the pendant she wore. It seemed no more than a humble trinket, yet you had secured the prize the Warchief desired so deeply, settling a bitter grudge from the past."}},[161]={k="495",["end"]={d=521,t="You ended the uprising born of a shiny trinket. Through Alterac's snows, you slew the Crushridge ogres and took the heads of Mug'Thol's lieutenants. At last, you executed the rebellious leader and took the Crown of Will from his corpse, returning it to the shadows of the Undercity. Lady Sylvanas has her prize, and the artifact that broke her mental hold is secure. The butchered ogres remain a brutal, silent monument: none may defy the Dark Lady and live."}},[196]={k="92401",["end"]={d=92401,t="You found Edward Heartweaver in the Ruins of Lordaeron and learned the fate he met while chasing ghosts, burdened by guilt over a son lost to Arthas's wrath. You carried the grim truth to his desperate wife, who had sent you to find him. The news brought her sorrow, but also bitter closure. Though grief remained, she no longer had to wonder what had become of her husband."}},[229]={k="581",["end"]={d=592,t="You searched Stranglethorn for a lost Darkspear son, gathering Bloodscalp heads to bargain with severed spirits. To make them speak, you broke the Skullsplitter chief. They told you young Yenniku had been enslaved by the outcast Zanzil. You struck down the ogre mage Mai'Zoth and claimed the Mind's Eye, then forged it into a Soul Gem. With it, you broke Zanzil's hold and trapped the boy's freed spirit within. You delivered Yenniku to Nimboya, rescuing the chieftain's blood from eternal darkness. Your victory earned a place in Darkspear legend, carved into stone forever."},mid={d=586,t="You searched Stranglethorn for Yenniku, the lost son of a Darkspear chief, at Nimboya's urging. Fearing the Bloodscalp tribe had taken him, you fought through their headhunters and gathered their trophies to see whether the boy's face was among them. None brought an answer. You then took the heads of the Bloodscalp leaders, Gan'zulah and Nezzliok the Dire, and plunged their remains into a boiling cauldron to bind the chieftain's spirit. The bound spirit sent you against the rival Skullsplitters, and you shattered Ana'thek the Cruel to appease the furious ghost. Yet the dead gave you no truth. Yenniku's fate remains unknown."}},[232]={k="605",["end"]={d=600,t="In Stranglethorn's sweltering depths, you gathered crystals for an eager goblin merchant. At Crank Fizzlebub's behest, you hunted the hardened basilisks south of Zul'Kunda and took the rare Singing Crystals from their hides. The Venture Company was tearing at the hills near the Crystalvein Mine for the same glittering prize. You struck at its camps and reclaimed gems from its hands. Your blows loosened the company's greedy grip on the jungle just a fraction, while Crank Fizzlebub, a rival merchant, gained crystals to line his pockets."}},[238]={k="570",["end"]={d=573,t="You gathered wild reagents for Far Seer Mok'thardin in Stranglethorn Vale. You took the razor-sharp claws of Shadowmaw Panthers, a pristine tigress fang, vibrant feathers from Jungle Stalkers, and flawless sinew from an Elder Mistvale Gorilla. You fought through a ruthless naga expedition to draw water from an ancient, contested Holy Spring. The Far Seer's shamanic rituals bound these things into a powerful enchanted choker. You wear it now, bearing the jungle's untamed magic in service to the Warchief and the Horde."}},[239]={k="595",["end"]={d=608,t="You began as a scout for First Mate Crazz, tracking rumors along the Savage Coast. A map detailing a Bloodsail invasion of Booty Bay drew you into a deadly shadow war. You infiltrated their camp on the Wild Shore, stole their charts, and uncovered Firallon's grand design. With that knowledge, you struck the true blow, then traveled to the cape and assassinated the Bloodsail leadership before their ships could raise anchor. The Blackwater Raiders now rule Booty Bay without dispute. By your hand alone, an entire pirate fleet lies broken and adrift, headless of its leaders."}},[243]={k="624",["end"]={d=626,t="You followed a dead pirate's rhyming riddle across two continents in search of hidden wealth. A damp scroll beneath a bridge in the Swamp of Sorrows led you to a musty parchment in a dangerous Dustwallow Marsh cave. Together, they revealed Cortello's final game. The trail ended in the rushing waters beneath the great falls of the Hinterlands, where you broke open the sunken chest in the shadowed depths. The long hunt ended there, and the legendary treasure was yours."}},[280]={k="1111",["end"]={d=1122,t="You crossed continents to enrich Kravel Koalbeard, skimming gnome parts in Ratchet and trading Swamp of Sorrows dream dust for blackmail on a racer. Crank Fizzlebub’s tainted brew, laced with Zanzil's poison, secured the grand prize. You slipped the Fool's Stout to a racing pit boss, rigging the odds and shattering an engine. The bets were cashed, and the gold flowed freely. Your scheme was complete, its ruin bought for a simple cut of the profits."},mid={d=1116,t="You started as a simple courier for Kravel Koalbeard, fetching delayed shipments from Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet. But Kravel proved true to his opportunistic nature. After pocketing a choice piece of machinery from the delivery intended for Fizzle Brassbolts, his schemes shifted from petty theft to blackmail. He set his sights on Nazz Steamboil, a goblin racer in the Shimmering Flats hiding behind a false name. Tracking down this secret sent you far to the south, seeking Krazek in the bustling port of Booty Bay. The rumormonger demanded a steep price for his whispers, forcing you into the murky Swamp of Sorrows to harvest dream dust from dragon whelps. You delivered the coveted snuff into Krazek's hands, yet the dark truth behind the racer's discarded identity remains locked away in the rumormonger's greedy mind."}},[2]={k="511",["end"]={d=537,t="You found an encrypted letter on a Syndicate table in Alterac, unaware of the dark ties it concealed. When Loremaster Dibbs could not break its cipher, you went to Ironforge, where Prospector Stormpike revealed its meaning. In Southshore, the translated text showed Magistrate Henry Maleb a sinister alliance with the Argus Wake. At his order, you entered the Uplands, killed the shadow mages, and executed their master, Nagaz. His death brought little comfort: Nagaz served another power, and the Argus Wake's shadowy grip may already reach across the world."}},[5]={k="522",["end"]={d=523,t="You found a sealed contract marking Magistrate Maleb for death and carried the grim news to Southshore. Its red wax bore the Syndicate mark, pointing to Baron Vardus, the cruel noble of fallen Alterac. You tracked the treacherous noble through ruined Strahnbrad and met his brutality with your own steel. With Vardus dead, you cut short the lingering plot. The magistrate rests easier, and the treacherous nobles of a ruined kingdom have learned that striking from the shadows brings justice."}},[13]={k="642A",["end"]={d=656,t="You freed Myzrael from the stones beneath the Arathi Highlands, believing her trapped and helpless. She was a dark entity revered by the Twilight's Hammer, chained by the giants for good reason. To undo your mistake, you found Theldurin the Lost in the Badlands and rebuilt the scroll that summoned her. At the Shards of Myzrael, you dragged her to the surface, struck her down, and bound her with eldritch shackles. Her wail still echoes from the deep, and the crystal pulses with malice. You corrected your error, but the earth still trembles."}},[14]={k="642H",["end"]={d=656,t="You freed Myzrael, a trapped earth princess, from the ancient stones forged by giants. Her gratitude was a lie, and you unleashed a dark terror allied with the maddened Twilight's Hammer. To right your wrong, you followed the rambling Theldurin the Lost into the Badlands and pieced together a torn scroll to force her hand. At the crystalline shards where she first deceived you, you dragged Myzrael to the surface and struck her down. Her eldritch shackles hold her deep beneath the Arathi Highlands once more. The earth groans with her fury, but the surface remains safe."}},[30]={k="720",["end"]={d=721,t="You followed a desperate plea scrawled on a crumpled map to Prospector Ryedol. Fearing his friend Hammertoe had been dragged into Uldaman by the ruthless Shadowforge clan, Ryedol urged you to mount a rescue. The Dark Irons wanted the captive dwarf's knowledge of titan excavations to forge terrible new golems, a threat Ironforge could not ignore. You fought through the ancient ruins and found Hammertoe battered, coughing, and barely clinging to life, yet immensely relieved. You reached him before his mind was broken and kept the titans' secrets from the enemy."}},[31]={k="707",["end"]={d=704,t="You searched the Badlands for the missing prospector and found shattered bones beside a bloody message in the dirt, written as he died. In honor of Agmond's grim end, you pressed into the Uldaman excavation and recovered the ancient urns he had died trying to unearth. The dusty relics now rest safely in scholarly hands. Agmond met a brutal fate, but his final discovery gave you a vital clue to understanding the savage troggs and the dark history buried beneath the stone."}},[32]={k="710",["end"]={d=778,t="In the scorched Badlands, you gathered stone from the earth's denizens for Lotwil Veriatus's dangerous ambition. You chipped away shards and claimed heavy binding bracers from towering rock giants, feeding his volatile arcane engineering. When Lucien Tosselwrench handed over the final cog and fled for cover, his terror was entirely justified. The arrogant mage's grand shackles failed spectacularly, releasing a raging monstrosity instead of an obedient servant. You stood firm and broke the destructive force before it could wreak havoc. Lotwil's groundbreaking history became another foolish disaster, and you were left to clean up the pieces."}},[33]={k="718",["end"]={d=717,t="You helped Sigrun Ironhew recover abandoned supplies from scavenging ogres, then caught the eye of Garek, an agent of the Kirin Tor. He sent you to retrieve the stolen Sign of the Earth, and you learned it bound Blacklash and Hematus, two of Deathwing's ruthless lieutenants. Their prison in Lethlor Ravine was no longer secure, so you shattered the ancient seal and drew out the black drakes. You ended their lives for good, leaving the skies safe from their ancient wrath and the Kirin Tor able to rest easy."}},[34]={k="709A",["end"]={d=737,t="You returned from Uldaman with the Tablet of Ryun'eh, but Theldurin's terrors remained. Bearing a dark sigil, you entered a secret brotherhood in Ironforge and traded relics of forbidden power to Gerrig Bonegrip for Yagyin's Digest. The cursed book now rested in Theldurin's trembling hands, giving him the knowledge he had begged for and a fragile weapon against ancient beings stirring beneath the earth. Whether that knowledge could spare the world from becoming worm food, or only delay its doom, remained unknown."}},[35]={k="709H",["end"]={d=737,t="You braved Uldaman's ancient depths and found the Tablet of Ryun'eh in a forgotten chest. Stone fragments alone could not calm the terrified dwarf. With his false sigil, you entered the Undercity and traded relics of power to Keeper Bel'dugur for a dark, secret tome. Now Theldurin clutches Yagyin's Digest in trembling hands, seeking salvation in its forbidden pages. You gave him a glimmer of hope against an unnamed doom sleeping beneath the earth. Whether this buried truth can save the world from ruin or hasten its end remains unknown."}},[36]={k="723",["end"]={d=762,t="You carried a dying dwarf's final plea from the Badlands to Ironforge. Hammertoe Grez gave everything to keep Uldaman's lost artifacts from Shadowforge hands. Through Prospector Ryedol and Historian Karnik, his amulet revealed a grave threat, and Advisor Belgrum swiftly blessed your strike. In Angor Fortress, you killed Ambassador Infernus, Ragnaros's fiery envoy. His defeat crippled the Shadowforge operations. Ironforge now prepares to reclaim its excavation site, while its people remain safeguarded by the burden you bore for a fallen explorer."}},[73]={k="1382",["end"]={d=1380,t="You sided with the Gelkis and shed their rivals' blood to prove your worth. You starved the Magram and humiliated the Kolkar, then traveled to the distant Swamp of Sorrows and claimed a crystal of alien magic for Uthek the Wise. Empowered by your gifts, you cut off Khan Jehn's head. Finally, high in the Valley of Spears, you sounded a stolen horn to draw out Khan Hratha of the Maraudine. His death broke their clan. The Gelkis now stand poised to rule the dusty plains of Desolace, and the spirits of the earth will echo your name forever."}},[74]={k="1385",["end"]={d=1381,t="You raised the Magram clan above Desolace's warring centaur tribes. To prove your strength to Warug, you slaughtered the Kolkar and shattered the Gelkis' sacred crystals. You brought the brute a strange mechanical toy, then turned against the enemy leaders. You severed Khan Shaka's head, summoned Khan Hratha, the Maraudine chieftain, and slew him, claiming his key. The Magram became the wasteland's undisputed masters. You secured safety for the strongholds, and Warug promised that you alone would be spared when centaur hooves trampled all others."}},[75]={k="1367",["end"]={d=1381,t="You joined the Magram in a brutal alliance sealed in Gelkis blood. You shattered the tears of Theradras to break their rivals' faith, appeased the hulking Warug with a mechanical trinket, and brought him Khan Shaka's severed head. Then you entered the Valley of Spears, sounded a stolen horn, and slaughtered Khan Hratha of the Maraudine. Their greatest enemies crushed, the Magram now dominate the desolate wastes. You gave them the reins to this barren land and won a rare promise: when their stampede begins, you alone will be spared."}},[76]={k="1368",["end"]={d=1380,t="You allied with the Gelkis to end the centaur wars of Desolace. You starved their Magram rivals, then crossed to a distant swamp and took a strange red crystal from the lost one Ongeku for Uthek the Wise. Her magic empowered you to kill Khan Jehn and sever the Magram's head. In the Valley of Spears, you sounded a stolen horn to draw out Khan Hratha, leader of the Maraudine. You killed him and claimed his key fragment. The rival clans are broken, and the Gelkis stand poised to conquer the wastes."}},[79]={k="1480",["end"]={d=1488,t="A flayed-skin contract sent you after Lord Azrethoc. To find him, you took a scalp from a Hatefury satyr and a flawless crystal from the coastal naga. The scrying ritual revealed a monster of terrible power, and his execution fell to you. You marched south and struck down the demon lord and his warlock servant in the dust. Azrethoc's grip on the Burning Blade is forever broken. Your victory crippled the Warchief's enemies, leaving the Horde's future in this desolate land a little brighter."}},[82]={k="6141",["end"]={d=1053,t="You crossed the sea to Desolace to seek a righteous war with Brother Anton. In the Valley of Bones, you shattered the rotting dead to prove your devotion and earned a seal of commendation for the Scarlet Crusade. When you carried it east to Southshore, Raleigh the Devout revealed the bitter truth: the Crusade's holy war had become a paranoid slaughter, with innocents tortured in the name of the Light. You chose not to join them. Instead, you broke into their monastery and ended their deranged regime, stopping a creeping madness and sparing countless lives from the pyre."}},[107]={k="1238",["end"]={d=7541,t="You dug an agent's severed head from the swamp muck and sought Darkspear dark magic to give his spirit a voice. Through a bubbling cauldron, Marg Nighteye confessed his final failure. You hunted the beast that killed him and recovered his prize, a glittering pendant of noble human craftsmanship held by mere soldiers near Theramore. Now the jewel rests in Orgrimmar with Zor Lonetree, while scholars have only just begun studying its origins. You honored a fallen spy's last wish and placed a piece of a dangerous Alliance mystery in Horde hands."}},[108]={k="1251",["end"]={d=1276,t="You pried a heavy, blackened iron shield from the charred chimney of the ruined Shady Rest Inn. Hoping it would reveal who attacked, you brought it to Krog, who gave it to the blacksmith Do'gol. You gathered venom from the marsh's giant spiders to scour away the soot, uncovering the name Mosarn. The trail led high into Thunder Bluff, where you questioned the craftsman. He recognized his work, but the revelation only frustrated you: he had forged too many pieces to remember one buyer. The shield left you with no answer, and the ashes of the inn remained unavenged."}},[110]={k="1321",["end"]={d=1276,t="You brought Krog a heavy, scorched shield, hoping its blackened metal held answers. When Do'gol the blacksmith needed solvent to clear the soot, you gathered acidic venom from the marsh's massive Darkfang spiders. The venom revealed one name etched into the shield's rim: Mosarn. You carried that clue to Thunder Bluff and found the master craftsman. Mosarn recognized his own handiwork, but his memory of the shield's owner was blank. Despite all your efforts, the truth stayed hidden, and the trail went cold."}},[111]={k="1260",["end"]={d=1271,t="You left Stormwind's taverns behind to help craft a menu for the Blue Recluse. In Dustwallow Marsh, you hunted mudrock turtles for their rare tongues, then traveled to the distant Swamp of Sorrows for flawless crab legs from beasts in its waters. The work was grueling, and the bogs were the world's most unforgiving. When you returned from the mud, Angus Stern welcomed you with a grand feast in your honor. That feast cemented your place as a celebrated guest at the finest table in the city."}},[113]={k="1252",["end"]={d=1287,t="You found a charred badge in the rubble, marked with Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name. When you brought it to Theramore's guards, you uncovered the bitter truth: Reethe had deserted, yet remained loyal to the late Admiral Daelin. You followed his former comrades to the ruins of Lost Point, where you learned they had cast him out for recklessly provoking the nearby ogres. Theramore now prepares to march on the deserters' camp and hunt down the rogue lieutenant. The discovery has brought a purge of the marsh's dissidents."}},[114]={k="1259",["end"]={d=1287,t="You uncovered the truth behind Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name. Adjutant Tesoran's records called the Kul Tiras marine distinguished and marked him missing, but Captain Vimes knew he was a traitor, fanatically loyal to Admiral Daelin. You tracked the deserters to an abandoned watchtower at Lost Point and broke their leader, Balos Jacken. He confessed they had abandoned Reethe after he recklessly planned to raid the ogres of Brackenwall Village. You carried this intelligence to Theramore. Now the guard marches against the deserter camp, and Reethe's days in the marsh are numbered."}},[116]={k="1169",["end"]={d=1173,t="You traced the threat to Onyxia's brood and shattered the dragonlord's eggs in the Wyrmbog. The Stonemaul Clan had been driven from their home by the beasts, and you gathered their remains so Draz'Zilb could identify the danger. When Overlord Mok'Morokk cowered before the black dragonflight, you struck at its spreading menace yourself. With the breeding grounds destroyed, you turned on Mok'Morokk and battered him until he fled into the marsh. Now the ogres are free to choose a worthy leader and march south to reclaim their stolen village."}},[117]={k="783",["end"]={d=54,t="You answered Stormwind's call while its armies were stretched thin. Marshal McBride ordered you to clear kobolds from the Echo Ridge Mine, driving back the thieves before they could deepen their foothold in Northshire. Then you carried sealed documents south to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire and became Acting Deputy. It was a grim promotion: with the true army entangled in the distant whims of nobles, Elwynn Forest's safety rested heavily on your shoulders."}},[125]={k="2862",["end"]={d=7732,t="You culled the desperate Woodpaw gnolls outside Camp Mojache and found they were fleeing a greater nightmare. Their crude battle plans led you south to the Writhing Deep, where an unknown enemy swarmed. Inside the insect hive, you slew the massive Stinglasher and gathered its glands for study. You carried the grim intelligence to Orgrimmar and brought the truth to Zilzibin Drumlore: silithid were driving the gnolls, an ancient horror the Horde had foolishly ignored. You secured the outpost, but uncovered a subterranean menace far greater than any petty faction war."}},[126]={k="2866",["end"]={d=2871,t="You returned to Feathermoon Stronghold and mounted an offensive against the Hatecrest naga. You had gone to the Ruins of Solarsal to learn why they swarmed the ancient stones, where you found a warm, glyph-carved gazebo. You slaughtered the serpentine invaders for their scales, then crossed the water to the Isle of Dread and assassinated Lord Shalzaru. With the cruel royal dead, the Hatecrest threat was broken, buying the stronghold precious time. The strange, alien relic you tore from his hands now rests with Vestia Moonspear, leaving an unsettling mystery in her care."}},[130]={k="4124",["end"]={d=4267,t="You found Raschal by following his trail from a shattered rowboat to the Woodpaw gnoll camps. Strange magic and abandoned baggage led you into the Writhing Deep, where you freed him from an alien Zukk'ash pod. Saving the courier revealed a greater danger. General Shandris Feathermoon sent you to Darnassus with a report of the infestation, and Gracina Spiritmight revealed that the insects were silithid. Your rescue in Feralas exposed a menace threatening to consume everything."},mid={d=4130,t="You began your search for a lost courier with Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold. Along Feralas’s coast, you found Raschal’s rowboat shattered in the shallows and his knife beneath the muddy water. Ginro sent you to Quintis Jonespyre, a druid who could draw history from the blade. Through psychometry, Quintis witnessed Raschal’s final known moments. The courier had clashed with Woodpaw gnolls, yet the beasts had not filled him with terror. Nor had the water elementals rising from the depths behind him. You brought this grim vision to Ginro, confirming that Raschal had faced a darker threat. What truly frightened him, and what fate he met in the wilds, remained unknown."}},[133]={k="3121",mid={d=3124,t="You brought a dwarven shrunken head to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow and exchanged it for a potent herbal mixture. Witch Doctor Uzer'i used the herbs to enchant a vessel meant to trap a dying creature's essence. You carried the artifact to the Hinterlands and tested it on Elune's savage owlbeasts. Only after they fell did you bind their spirits, trapping their muisek before vengeance could find them. You then captured the souls of the noble frayfeather hippogryphs in the same way. Now Uzer'i holds the trapped essence of these fierce, wild creatures in his hands. You have learned this dangerous art, but what the witch doctor means to do with the power he gathered remains unknown."},["end"]={d=3129,t="You brought a shrunken head to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar and received the herbs needed to trap souls. With Uzer'i's prepared muisek vessel, you hunted the ancient forests of the Hinterlands, slaying sacred allies of the night elves. You bound the vengeful spirits of fierce owlbeasts and loyal hippogryphs, trapped elusive faerie dragons, and felled ancient wandering treants. You brought down towering mountain giants before their essence could flee. Uzer'i forged these captive spirits into mortal steel, chaining the fallen protectors' primal strength to your hands and empowering the Horde."}},[134]={k="3125",["end"]={d=3129,t="You captured the strength of the wilderness for the Horde, taking the spirits of the night elves' ancient allies. You stripped magical essence from delicate sprite darters and protective souls from lumbering wandering forest walkers. Then you felled towering mountain giants, and Witch Doctor Uzer'i trapped their massive power in his vessels. His dark ritual bound that stolen strength into steel and wood. You left with the might of the forest itself, wielding a heavy weapon forged from captured souls."}},[137]={k="2939",["end"]={d=2942,t="You carried a mysterious stave from Feralas's overgrown ruins to Darnassus, seeking answers. To get a history book from Daryn Lightwind, you traveled the world with Curgle Cranklehop's crude camera and captured a massive turtle in the Hinterlands. When you returned to Troyas Moonbreeze, the knowledge you had earned revealed the stave's true purpose. With ancient fire, you entered the Ruins of Ravenwind and awakened the Equinex Monolith. From its cold heart, you took the Morrow Stone. Its full power remained a mystery, but you had uncovered a relic of immense significance and rescued a piece of ancient history from the wilds."}},[138]={k="2969",["end"]={d=4298,t="You freed the faerie dragons from Grimtotem cages in Feralas alongside the Moonweavers, and your deeds reached High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. But your journey came to rest on a fragile egg. You carried it across the world to the distant Hinterlands, seeking the wisdom of Quentin and Agnar, the beast handler. You gathered fresh meat to keep the unborn sprite darter alive and guarded it until the shell broke. A tiny, winged life emerged, safe in your care as its new guardian."},mid={d=3841,t="In Feralas, you freed the captive faerie dragons with the Moonweaver sisters. You broke the Grimtotem clan's cruel cages, then struck at the tauren camp in retribution for their poaching. Your path took you to the boughs of Teldrassil, where you gave Jer'kai's signet ring to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. She sent scouts to watch over the sisters, but your part in the tale continued. You brought Quentin a rare, nearly mature sprite darter egg, saving the orphan from the same poachers you had slaughtered. Now the fragile egg rests before you, full of life. Will the tiny creature hatch safely and survive to spread its wings?"}},[159]={k="659",["end"]={d=661,t="Stanley's savage mutation as a dog drew you into Forsaken intrigue in Hillsbrad. At Phin Odelic's behest, you searched the Arathi Highlands for his missing companions. You found Quae and Kinelory watching Go'Shek Farm, intercepted a courier, and uncovered Apothecary Jorell's grim experiments. You fought beside Kinelory to raid the farm and take the remaining research, then carried the evidence safely back to Southshore. The full scope of the undead's sinister work remains unknown, but Phin has the proof he needs. By your blade, the plague spreaders suffered a heavy blow, and three friends live to fight another day."}},[162]={k="1450",["end"]={d=1469,t="You found Brohann Caskbelly's lost expedition in the memory of a disgraced rider. Falstad Wildhammer sent you to Gryphon Master Talonaxe, who remembered Rhapsody Shindigger as a brilliant rider ruined by drink. You found him at a remote camp, lost in ale, and crossed the sea to Kalimdor for beasts in Tanaris and Feralas. Their hunt gave you ingredients for a fierce concoction that stirred Rhapsody's memory of falling drunk into a swamp. He recalled a sunken temple swarming with trolls. You returned his stolen Atal'ai artifact to Brohann, proving the ancient ruins lay beneath dark waters."}},[188]={k="1109",["end"]={d=1113,t="You descended into the muck of Razorfen Kraul, scraping foul guano from the roosts of the rare Kraul Bats. But the Royal Apothecary Society required more than mere filth for their grand experiment. You marched to the peaks of Tirisfal Glades, butchering the fanatical members of the Scarlet Crusade within the Scarlet Monastery to tear the beating hearts from their chests. Now, you have delivered these bloody prizes to the Master. In these shadowed halls, clashing elements will be fused with deadly toxins. You have provided the catalyst for a new, ghastly creation born of blind zealotry and festering decay."}},[199]={k="3441",["end"]={d=3481,t="You became Kalaran Windblade's instrument of vengeance against the Dark Iron dwarves. You gathered elemental flames, shattered thorium blades, and stole a heathen idol to forge the Torch of Retribution, meant to cripple their defenses. Its raw hatred pulsed through your veins when you grasped it. Guided by Squire Maltrake, you carried that spite into the enemy's sentry towers and engulfed them in an inextinguishable blaze. The dwarven lines broke, their fortifications swallowed by fire. At last, you claimed your prize from a black dragon's hoard, left to wonder who had truly orchestrated this devastation."},mid={d=3452,t="Kalaran Windblade drew you into his grim scheme for vengeance. He planned to reduce four sentry towers to ash and strike a crippling blow against his foes. Ordinary fire would not suffice, so you hunted elementals and golems across the wastes for their fiery hearts and oil. You took enchanted thorium daggers from brutal Dark Iron slavers and forged a sturdy shaft. Then you climbed the mountains and slew Twilight's Hammer cultists, claiming a dark symbol of Ragnaros for the torch's magical casing. With the foul magic secured, the torch was whole, and you held the means to ignite the towers. What consequences Kalaran's retribution would bring remained unknown."}},[223]={k="1274",["end"]={d=1247,t="Young Thomas sent you to Bishop DeLavey and drew you into a quiet conspiracy. A diplomat bound for Theramore had vanished without a trace. You carried sealed letters from Jorgen to cheesemaker Elling Trias, following whispers to Watcher Backus in Duskwood. At Addle's Stead, you uncovered Defias documents outlining a sinister plot. Its final piece came only after you beat the truth out of Dashel Stonefist in an alley. His bloody confession revealed a backup plan run by an inside man named Slim. You had cracked the plot wide open, but the desperate search had shifted to Menethil."},mid={d=1243,t="A quiet word from young Thomas drew you into the shadowed halls of Stormwind Keep. There, Bishop DeLavey entrusted you with a heavy secret: a diplomat bound for Theramore had vanished without a trace. Suspecting the Defias, the bishop directed you to his hidden contacts. You found the grudging Jorgen in the Valley of Heroes, who passed a sealed note for you to carry to Elling Trias in the Trade District. The cheesemaker quickly dropped his guise of a simple merchant, tapping into his covert network to point you down a much darker road. Now you stand under the gloomy canopy of Duskwood, questioning Watcher Backus about recent Defias movements. But the fate of the missing diplomat, and the true depths of the conspiracy that stole them away, still remain hidden in the shadows."}},[225]={k="583",["end"]={d=208,t="You came to Stranglethorn as a stranger, seeking Hemet Nesingwary's wisdom. To prove your worth, you thinned the raptor packs in the thick foliage, then claimed the talon of the cunning Tethis. After matching wits with the jungle's finest predators, you set your sights on the expedition's ultimate prize. Deep in the wilderness, you cornered and slew the legendary white tiger, King Bangalash. You returned with this final trophy and earned the absolute respect of a renowned war hero. Your mastery of the hunt is now unquestioned."}},[227]={k="215",["end"]={d=331,t="You rescued Private Thorsen and learned he had a secret mission to infiltrate Kurzen's forces. After realizing a traitor had exposed him, you searched Bookie Herod's records and found a hidden key. In the enemy stockpile, you opened a secure strongbox and discovered a muddy note that tracked Thorsen's every move. You compared the camp's patrol schedules with the letter's signature and unmasked Private Merle as the informant. The betrayal cut deep, but you purged a deadly rot from the rebel ranks. Without a spy feeding their secrets to a corrupt colonel, these desperate outcasts finally stand a chance."}},[231]={k="2842",["end"]={d=2843,t="Kernobee's discovery sent you seeking a swift path to Gnomeregan. You crossed the sea from Ratchet to Booty Bay's tropical shores, where you found Scooty and his volatile Transpolyporter 6000. Though the goblin reassured you about its explosive history, you let him calibrate a personal transponder to your exact size and weight. The perilous overland trek through Dun Morogh's frozen, dwarf-infested peaks was behind you. One brave step onto the pad, and Gnomeregan's irradiated depths awaited you in a blinding flash, continents bridged in a heartbeat."}},[236]={k="616",["end"]={d=611,t="A rumor in Booty Bay sent you after a fabled troll relic. You braved a haunted island off Stranglethorn and found Gazban, a cursed goblin mage. To break his affliction, you brought elemental remnants to Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver in Dalaran. His counsel sent you back to his pirate daughter Catelyn, who needed you to reclaim an ancient dagger from a Bloodsail Buccaneer. Beneath the waves, you plunged the blade into a sunken altar and shattered the enchantment. After delivering the Stone of the Tides to Baron Revilgaz, you left the magnificent Gurubashi artifact secure in his private collection."}},[240]={k="606",["end"]={d=613,t="You settled Sea Wolf MacKinley's ledgers by ruthless means. You preyed on Shaky Phillipe's fears, using gorilla gore to extort coin, then hunted through the cursed ruins of Aboraz and Jubuwal to claim the undead's dues. Maury Wilkins's locked club foot had to be severed, and you fought through the Mosh'Ogg ogre mound to find its key. At last, the dead man's hollow leg was cracked open, and MacKinley received his bloody prize. The debts are settled; your pockets are heavy, and your hands forever stained."}},[247]={k="9609",["end"]={d=1425,t="You found Watcher Biggs, sole survivor of a brutal Lost Ones ambush, stranded in the murky swamp. After holding back the wild beasts drawn to his ruined camp, you entered the Fallow Sanctuary and reclaimed the stolen reagents the Nethergarde wizards desperately needed. You gathered sun-dried driftwood from the eastern coast to repair his broken wagon, then carried the caravan's most vital supplies south into the desolate Blasted Lands. Delivering the salvaged crystals to Quartermaster Lungertz ensured Nethergarde Keep could continue its lonely, crucial watch over the Dark Portal. Because of you, the Alliance's defenses held strong."}},[248]={k="698",["end"]={d=1428,t="You journeyed to the desolate eastern coast, hauling fresh sawtooth meat to feed an isolated Horde outpost. To arm the camp, you harvested razor-sharp claws from the beasts, supplying Tok'Kar with the means to craft rugged weapons. But true security demanded a bloodier toll. Directed by Katar's bitter hatred for the ocean's spawn, you carved a relentless path through the murloc tribes polluting the shore. Their gurgling cries were silenced, their ranks broken upon the sand. You leave the beach soaked in the blood of the fish men, bearing a newly forged weapon as a grim token of your slaughter. The encroaching sea has been pushed back."}},[255]={k="992A",["end"]={d=162,t="You mapped dry wells for Gadgetzan and found a horror spreading through the sands. At the drained pools of the Noxious Lair and deep in the Gaping Chasm, you faced a swarm moved by a sinister, unseen will. There, you found the remains of a lost goblin. Alchemist Pestlezugg’s findings confirmed these were no mindless beasts. You carried the warning all the way to Darnassus, where Gracina Spiritmight named your enemy: the silithid. A dispute over desert water had exposed an ancient, ravenous menace threatening all of Kalimdor."}},[256]={k="992H",["end"]={d=32,t="You searched for water near Sandsorrow Watch and found a desert drained by ravenous insects. From the Centipaar in the Noxious Lair to the lost surveyor Scrimshank in the Gaping Chasm, you followed the creeping horror. Alchemist Pestlezugg confirmed that an unseen, malignant will drove these mindless ravagers. You carried this grim truth across the sands to Orgrimmar, where Zilzibin Drumlore gave the nightmare a name: the silithid had risen. What began as a simple drought had become an apocalyptic threat to all of Azeroth."}},[259]={k="8576",["end"]={d=8606,t="You found an empty hole south of Land's End Beach, where Narain Soothfancy had buried his translation manual. The ransom note pasted there crudely explained why it was gone. Azuregos’s ledger held the secrets of an ancient device, but its Draconic text still baffled Narain. Enraged by the extortion, he dressed you in his robes and a turban, then sent you into the freezing snows of Winterspring with a bag of rocks to spring a trap. The thieves slipped through your fingers. The ambush failed, the manual vanished, and you had gravely underestimated your unseen foes."}},[261]={k="8922",["end"]={d=8928,t="Deliana’s need to speak with Anthion Harmon’s ghost sent you to Mux Manascrambler. To fuel his work, you gathered what he needed from the world’s most perilous edges: volcanic ash for a distiller, the anguish of tortured spirits across three continents, and a beating magma core torn from an elemental lord. You braved a demon-infested gorge to secure a channeling rod. Mux assembled his intricate machine, and after the rod was secured, the veil between worlds was pierced. Now the dead are ready to speak."}},[262]={k="8923",["end"]={d=8928,t="You traveled to the ends of the world to gather components for Mux Manascrambler. From the Burning Steppes, you brought volcanic ash. Across Silithus, Winterspring, and the Plaguelands, you harvested haunted ectoplasm from tormented spirits. You tore a molten core from Magma Lord Bokk to power the device, then braved the depths of Darkwhisper Gorge to purchase a specialized channeling rod. At last, the machine was complete, built to pierce the veil of death. With its rare components united, the barrier between worlds had weakened, bringing Mokvar's desperate hope of speaking with the fallen Anthion within reach."}},[276]={k="1104",["end"]={d=1194,t="You helped Fizzle Brassbolts test his racing machines, finding scorpid venom for fuel and tracking down Martek the Exiled in the Badlands. Martek found that indurium flakes could withstand immense heat, sending the gnomes toward Uldaman in search of pure ore. But loyalty on the salt flats was fleeting. With Zamek drawing attention away, you entered the gnomes' camp and stole Rizzle Brassbolts' schematics. You gave the stolen indurium sample to Pozzik, putting both factions on equal footing. Now each side knows the metallic prize lies deep within the earth, and their fierce rivalry will burn hotter than ever."}},[278]={k="1176",["end"]={d=1189,t="You gathered vulture bones from the salt flats to lighten Pozzik's racers. When the promised fuel regulator vanished, you followed its trail from Gazlowe in Ratchet to the wharves of Booty Bay. You stole the blueprints from under Cozzle's nose and gave the goblin team the edge they wanted. Yet Razzeric, their reckless pilot, needed more than engineering. You salvaged a volatile seaforium booster from a crashed zeppelin and took it to Shreev in Gadgetzan to remove its safety limits. Now a madman has a bomb strapped to an engine, and the great rivalry has changed forever."},mid={d=1182,t="You reached the salt flats seeking speed, gathering bones to lighten Pozzik’s machines. Lighter frames alone could not assure victory over the gnomes, so the goblin needed a prototype fuel regulator. You chased its trail across the sea. Gazlowe in Ratchet had no answers, and Wharfmaster Lozgil found only empty ledgers in Booty Bay. Baron Revilgaz finally admitted the regulator had never been built. You entered the Stranglethorn jungles and broke into Cozzle's home to steal the Venture Company foreman's blueprints. Revilgaz claimed the schematics to make his own copies, readying you to return to the racers. The hard work was done, but the outcome remained unknown: would the stolen designs give Pozzik the edge he craved, or was his team doomed to eat gnome dust?"}},[303]={k="79008",["end"]={d=79980,t="A dying fire gave you the note that began this grim trail. It led you to a charred corpse and revealed botched New Plague deliveries disguised as apothecary accidents. You followed the dead man's directions into the rugged peaks between the Barrens and Desolace, then made a treacherous descent from his hidden camp. In the dirt, you found a buried messenger bag stocked with survival supplies and a soiled parchment. Its clues led you to a secret stash, proving the deadly conspiracy reached far beyond a few scattered ashes."}},[304]={k="463",["end"]={d=98283,t="You answered Rethiel the Greenwarden's call to heal the Wetlands' suffering ecosystem. Near the gates of Algaz, you culled the encroaching Mosshide gnolls and stripped away their flints to protect the living wood. When diseased fen creepers blistered the marsh, you laid the shambling horrors to rest. Beneath Raptor Ridge, you used malignant flesh to draw out Carnage, a maddened alpha raptor. Slaying the beast brought desperate peace to the Razormaw pack, and the wounded wetlands finally had time to mend."}}},
